1
00:02:41,964 --> 00:02:44,338
♪ The One, The One, The One...
Say... ♪

2
00:02:44,339 --> 00:02:46,630
♪ He's a tiger that roars
like sudden thunder ♪

3
00:02:46,631 --> 00:02:49,296
♪ The One, The One, The One...
Say... ♪

4
00:02:49,297 --> 00:02:51,588
♪ With fireworks raging,
burning in wrath ♪

5
00:02:51,589 --> 00:02:54,046
♪ Even the Devil bowed and fled,
His arrogance torn and ripped to shreds ♪

6
00:02:54,047 --> 00:02:57,297
♪ For He is the Ancient Ancestor,
The eternal, watchful protector ♪

7
00:03:16,922 --> 00:03:23,464
♪ One who stands tall and mighty,
upon the eighteenth step, O Karuppa ♪

8
00:03:38,506 --> 00:03:41,631
Lord Karuppa!

9
00:03:42,214 --> 00:03:45,380
♪ Behold, Karuppan arrives ♪

10
00:03:45,381 --> 00:03:48,630
♪ The fierce Karuppan emerges ♪

11
00:03:48,631 --> 00:03:51,881
♪ Behold, Karuppan arrives ♪

12
00:03:55,339 --> 00:03:58,505
♪ Lord Karuppa, manifest thy power ♪

13
00:03:58,506 --> 00:04:01,964
♪ Bestow Thy presence upon us ♪

14
00:04:21,506 --> 00:04:22,313
[in Malayalam]
What is it, Dad?

15
00:04:22,922 --> 00:04:24,131
[in Malayalam]
Err... Nothing.

16
00:04:26,339 --> 00:04:27,839
Why has the train stopped?

17
00:04:28,006 --> 00:04:29,464
It's been halted for 10 minutes.

18
00:04:29,589 --> 00:04:30,555
I have no idea where we are!

19
00:04:31,381 --> 00:04:32,359
Didn't you get any sleep, dear?

20
00:04:32,756 --> 00:04:34,051
- I woke up a little while ago.
- Alright!

21
00:04:34,714 --> 00:04:36,005
Does your phone have charge?

22
00:04:36,006 --> 00:04:37,046
Yeah, for now.

23
00:04:37,047 --> 00:04:38,773
If you keep staring at it,
the battery will die.

24
00:04:39,922 --> 00:04:41,005
What's your problem?

25
00:04:41,006 --> 00:04:42,630
See, it has charge.

26
00:04:42,631 --> 00:04:44,046
You're always fussing over
one thing or another!

27
00:04:44,047 --> 00:04:45,505
Check today's gold rate.

28
00:04:45,506 --> 00:04:47,005
That will drain the battery for sure.

29
00:04:47,006 --> 00:04:48,047
Oh, really?

30
00:04:48,422 --> 00:04:50,213
[in Tamil]
Sir, which station is this?

31
00:04:50,214 --> 00:04:51,463
This is Basin Bridge signal, sir.

32
00:04:51,464 --> 00:04:52,880
The train will halt here
for 45 minutes.

33
00:04:52,881 --> 00:04:54,588
- Where are you headed?
- Choolaimedu.

34
00:04:54,589 --> 00:04:55,630
Then you might as well get off here.

35
00:04:55,631 --> 00:04:57,288
See, there's an auto waiting.
You'll be there in no time.

36
00:04:58,131 --> 00:05:00,296
Oh, the auto is right here.
Dear, let's get off here. Thank you, sir.

37
00:05:00,297 --> 00:05:01,171
Get off here?

38
00:05:02,297 --> 00:05:03,421
Hurry up!

39
00:05:03,422 --> 00:05:04,248
Coming!

40
00:05:13,047 --> 00:05:14,714
- Watch your step, Dad.
- Okay.

41
00:05:25,714 --> 00:05:27,339
Sir, will you take us
to Choolaimedu?

42
00:05:27,547 --> 00:05:29,380
Sure, sir.
Where in Choolaimedu?

43
00:05:29,381 --> 00:05:30,630
We need to go to A.K. Lodge.

44
00:05:30,631 --> 00:05:31,755
It'll be 800 rupees.

45
00:05:31,756 --> 00:05:33,796
For 800 rupees, I could
go to Kerala and come back!

46
00:05:33,797 --> 00:05:35,421
Then why don't you go back
to Kerala, sir?

47
00:05:35,422 --> 00:05:38,005
Isn't that a bit much?
Just cross-check it on your phone.

48
00:05:38,006 --> 00:05:38,796
Check if this is correct.

49
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:41,046
- This auto won't come, sir. Go now.
- Okay, let's go.

50
00:05:41,047 --> 00:05:43,421
- Hey, don't go. I'll give you money.
- Hey! Hey!

51
00:05:43,422 --> 00:05:44,546
Hey!

52
00:05:44,547 --> 00:05:46,255
- Hey! Shut up!
- Dad! Dad!

53
00:05:46,256 --> 00:05:47,921
- Don't scream!
- Let go!

54
00:05:47,922 --> 00:05:50,506
- Hand over the chain!
- Don't hurt her!

55
00:05:51,214 --> 00:05:52,297
Get that knife away!

56
00:05:53,214 --> 00:05:54,214
Dad!

57
00:05:56,839 --> 00:05:57,963
Let go of her!

58
00:05:57,964 --> 00:06:00,256
- Sir, please! Let us go!
- Let us go!

59
00:06:00,922 --> 00:06:03,921
Let go of the bag.

60
00:06:03,922 --> 00:06:05,296
- Don't take my bag!
- Dude, run!

61
00:06:05,297 --> 00:06:06,671
Give me my bag!

62
00:06:06,672 --> 00:06:08,130
My bag!

63
00:06:08,131 --> 00:06:09,922
Dad! Dad!!

64
00:06:13,006 --> 00:06:14,714
Please... give me my bag.

65
00:06:15,131 --> 00:06:17,131
Please give me my bag!

66
00:06:17,589 --> 00:06:19,547
Please, don't take it...

67
00:06:19,964 --> 00:06:22,172
There is nothing of value in it!

68
00:06:31,756 --> 00:06:33,671
Your story doesn't quite add up.

69
00:06:33,672 --> 00:06:35,589
You claim this is your
first time in Chennai,

70
00:06:36,047 --> 00:06:37,755
yet you chose to get off
at Basin Bridge?

71
00:06:37,756 --> 00:06:39,713
Shouldn't you have gotten off
at Central Station?

72
00:06:39,714 --> 00:06:40,921
There's no need to be afraid.
Tell me the truth.

73
00:06:40,922 --> 00:06:43,421
Who is this man?
Is he really your father?

74
00:06:43,422 --> 00:06:44,921
Or did he force you
to come with him?

75
00:06:44,922 --> 00:06:46,755
How can you say such
a thing, Madam?

76
00:06:46,756 --> 00:06:48,921
- She's my daughter!
- Hey! I'm talking to her, aren't I?

77
00:06:48,922 --> 00:06:49,964
You keep your mouth shut!

78
00:06:50,922 --> 00:06:52,255
Madam, this is very wrong.

79
00:06:52,256 --> 00:06:54,547
We came here to report
our bag being stolen.

80
00:06:54,756 --> 00:06:56,171
And you're harassing us instead?

81
00:06:56,172 --> 00:06:58,088
I'm recording this and
posting it on Instagram.

82
00:06:58,089 --> 00:06:59,296
Hey, put that phone away!
Put it down!

83
00:06:59,297 --> 00:07:01,005
Madam, put it away.
Please, put it away.

84
00:07:01,006 --> 00:07:03,171
Look at yourself, look at that dress.
Is that what you wear on a train?

85
00:07:03,172 --> 00:07:04,505
Couldn't you find
anything shorter?

86
00:07:04,506 --> 00:07:06,082
You should be grateful
it was only your jewellery you lost.

87
00:07:07,172 --> 00:07:09,338
You people are careless,
and we're the ones who suffer for it!

88
00:07:09,339 --> 00:07:10,863
Madam... please...

89
00:07:11,256 --> 00:07:13,172
Please, just find
our jewellery somehow.

90
00:07:13,797 --> 00:07:14,796
- Kumaran sir.
- Madam.

91
00:07:14,797 --> 00:07:15,944
Chains, earrings,
the whole lot...

92
00:07:16,214 --> 00:07:18,046
Get the weight in grams
and put it in writing.

93
00:07:18,047 --> 00:07:19,088
How many grams?

94
00:07:19,089 --> 00:07:20,714
Not grams, sovereigns!

95
00:07:20,839 --> 00:07:22,214
- Sovereigns?
- Yes!

96
00:07:23,547 --> 00:07:24,547
How many?

97
00:07:24,964 --> 00:07:26,422
Err... sixty!

98
00:07:27,006 --> 00:07:27,869
Sixty sovereigns.

99
00:07:35,297 --> 00:07:36,296
Hey!

100
00:07:36,297 --> 00:07:38,171
Who carries this much gold
on a train?

101
00:07:38,172 --> 00:07:39,214
Have you no sense at all?

102
00:07:39,756 --> 00:07:41,422
I thought I'd get a better price

103
00:07:41,756 --> 00:07:43,422
if I sold it at the current rate.

104
00:07:43,547 --> 00:07:44,880
By selling it for more,

105
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:46,881
are you planning to buy a house
near Dhanush's in Poes Garden?

106
00:07:49,214 --> 00:07:50,881
Your daughter has
had a liver failure.

107
00:07:51,464 --> 00:07:53,589
Her condition has worsened
since her last visit.

108
00:07:55,172 --> 00:07:57,006
The surgery needs to be
performed immediately.

109
00:07:57,297 --> 00:07:58,921
Your liver matches hers.

110
00:07:58,922 --> 00:08:00,547
But the transplant
is quite expensive.

111
00:08:00,922 --> 00:08:02,463
It may cost around 25 to 30 lakhs.

112
00:08:02,464 --> 00:08:03,671
Don't have the surgery done here.

113
00:08:03,672 --> 00:08:04,797
Get it done in Chennai.

114
00:08:04,922 --> 00:08:06,756
But the sooner, the better.

115
00:08:07,589 --> 00:08:10,006
Once blood appears
in her vomit or stool,

116
00:08:10,422 --> 00:08:11,922
surgery will be far more risky.

117
00:08:17,839 --> 00:08:19,380
- Sir?
- Hey, Mammootty!

118
00:08:19,381 --> 00:08:20,296
Why are you late?

119
00:08:20,297 --> 00:08:22,505
We've picked up all the usual suspects
and given them a good thrashing.

120
00:08:22,506 --> 00:08:24,422
Once you identify them,
we'll lock them up!

121
00:08:39,506 --> 00:08:40,119
Sir!

122
00:08:40,672 --> 00:08:42,589
We didn't do it, sir!
I swear!

123
00:08:42,964 --> 00:08:45,172
The police are beating
the life out of us.

124
00:08:45,631 --> 00:08:48,546
If you talk to them, they'll listen.
Please, tell them to let us go!

125
00:08:48,547 --> 00:08:49,293
Akka!

126
00:08:49,881 --> 00:08:51,672
I'm just a college student
like you, Akka!

127
00:08:52,006 --> 00:08:53,546
Why would I rob anyone?

128
00:08:53,547 --> 00:08:55,921
Look what they've done to me.

129
00:08:55,922 --> 00:08:57,671
- It hurts, Akka!
- It really hurts!

130
00:08:57,672 --> 00:08:59,005
Please believe us, sir.

131
00:08:59,006 --> 00:09:00,881
It was not us!
I swear!

132
00:09:06,381 --> 00:09:08,046
Yesterday, they were at
your feet, crying for mercy.

133
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:10,463
And they're the same guys
who pulled off a job like this.

134
00:09:10,464 --> 00:09:13,381
Hey Mammootty! Guys like this
don't deserve any mercy.

135
00:09:14,964 --> 00:09:16,796
I'm the one who managed
to wrap this up so fast.

136
00:09:16,797 --> 00:09:18,463
So, send me a little
something on GPay.

137
00:09:18,464 --> 00:09:19,395
Anyway, just sign here for now.

138
00:09:19,881 --> 00:09:22,047
Sir, a coin necklace and
a gold chain are missing.

139
00:09:22,172 --> 00:09:23,463
How can I sign
with items still missing?

140
00:09:23,464 --> 00:09:25,463
Together, they weigh
fifteen sovereigns.

141
00:09:25,464 --> 00:09:29,421
Sir, people spend ten years
trying to recover stolen gold.

142
00:09:29,422 --> 00:09:31,964
Be grateful you got yours back
so quickly. Just sign, sir.

143
00:09:33,547 --> 00:09:35,255
What's up, Chetta?
Happy now?

144
00:09:35,256 --> 00:09:36,546
Got all your gold back?

145
00:09:36,547 --> 00:09:37,881
How can I be happy, Madam?

146
00:09:38,047 --> 00:09:39,838
My coin necklace and chain
are still missing.

147
00:09:39,839 --> 00:09:41,296
- Without them--
- I'll slap you, old man.

148
00:09:41,297 --> 00:09:43,797
You think thieves just keep
your gold safe and return it?

149
00:09:44,089 --> 00:09:47,006
They took it to Mahabalipuram
that very night and blew the lot!

150
00:09:47,256 --> 00:09:49,131
Tell me, you guys had a
great time, didn't you?

151
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:50,815
Look at them nodding away.

152
00:09:52,297 --> 00:09:54,131
What now?
Do you want the gold or not?

153
00:09:54,922 --> 00:09:56,588
- Put it back in the locker, sir.
- Okay, Madam.

154
00:09:56,589 --> 00:09:58,756
No, Madam! Please, don't.
I'll sign the papers.

155
00:09:58,922 --> 00:10:00,006
Then sign and get going.

156
00:10:00,172 --> 00:10:02,089
He thinks they'll just hand it over
the moment he asks!

157
00:10:02,714 --> 00:10:04,463
I warned you,
but you wouldn't listen.

158
00:10:04,464 --> 00:10:05,589
I'll take this with me then.

159
00:10:05,714 --> 00:10:06,755
Hey, put that down.

160
00:10:06,756 --> 00:10:08,172
Put it down.
Put it down, sir.

161
00:10:08,464 --> 00:10:09,824
We aren't authorised
to hand this over here.

162
00:10:10,339 --> 00:10:11,171
Why is that, sir?

163
00:10:11,172 --> 00:10:13,046
You'll have to claim it
through the court.

164
00:10:13,047 --> 00:10:14,296
- What for?
- Yes, sir.

165
00:10:14,297 --> 00:10:15,338
That's the standard procedure.

166
00:10:15,339 --> 00:10:17,838
You must file a "Return of Property"
petition in court

167
00:10:17,839 --> 00:10:19,130
to get your stolen items back.

168
00:10:19,131 --> 00:10:21,921
Why go to court for gold
that's already been found?

169
00:10:21,922 --> 00:10:23,338
Sir, if we hand it over today,

170
00:10:23,339 --> 00:10:25,922
and you claim tomorrow that
you never got it, we'll be screwed.

171
00:10:26,089 --> 00:10:27,505
It's a simple matter, sir.

172
00:10:27,506 --> 00:10:29,797
Hire a solid lawyer
and you'll have it in no time.

173
00:10:30,214 --> 00:10:30,921
I'll help you.

174
00:10:32,672 --> 00:10:33,671
Here you go.

175
00:10:33,672 --> 00:10:34,880
He's a top-tier lawyer.

176
00:10:34,881 --> 00:10:36,713
Tell them Kumaran sir from the station
gave you the lead.

177
00:10:36,714 --> 00:10:39,546
♪ Our flag across the town shall soar,
While sparks and crackers loudly roar ♪

178
00:10:39,547 --> 00:10:46,006
♪ Red-carpet entry for the native son,
With his gang behind him, second to none ♪

179
00:10:48,047 --> 00:10:49,395
Please, sir!

180
00:10:49,672 --> 00:10:50,838
Look at the time, it's 10:30.

181
00:10:50,839 --> 00:10:52,463
Get moving, get moving.
That's it.

182
00:10:52,464 --> 00:10:53,380
Go! Go!

183
00:10:53,381 --> 00:10:55,380
None of you ever show up on time.
Get going!

184
00:10:55,381 --> 00:10:56,797
- 43
- Hey, Bench.

185
00:10:56,922 --> 00:10:59,255
Hey! Have you ever shown up
on time even once?

186
00:10:59,256 --> 00:11:01,338
You think being on Baby Kannan's team
gives you a free pass?

187
00:11:01,339 --> 00:11:03,832
Baby Sir is right here.
You want to say that to his face?

188
00:11:04,089 --> 00:11:06,256
Alright, hand it over.
Don't say a word to him. Go!

189
00:11:15,547 --> 00:11:16,547
Be seated.

190
00:11:21,631 --> 00:11:22,922
What's with the flowers
and the silk saree?

191
00:11:23,297 --> 00:11:24,546
Are you here for a wedding?

192
00:11:24,547 --> 00:11:25,963
Have you even
seen your own face?

193
00:11:25,964 --> 00:11:27,713
CC 2943

194
00:11:27,714 --> 00:11:29,255
Sankaran, Sakunthala...

195
00:11:29,256 --> 00:11:30,797
versus Stone Brothers.

196
00:11:31,089 --> 00:11:32,381
Preethi, you can proceed.

197
00:11:36,839 --> 00:11:37,887
What's your prayer, Preethi?

198
00:11:38,214 --> 00:11:41,005
My Lord...
My clients, Mr. and Mrs. Sankaran,

199
00:11:41,006 --> 00:11:44,963
leased their property
to these four individuals in 2007.

200
00:11:44,964 --> 00:11:46,921
Operating as G.D. Biscuit Factory,

201
00:11:46,922 --> 00:11:48,713
long after their lease expired,

202
00:11:48,714 --> 00:11:51,380
they have continued to occupy
and run the premises.

203
00:11:51,381 --> 00:11:54,005
In response, my clients
filed an eviction suit.

204
00:11:54,006 --> 00:11:55,380
To cover their tracks,

205
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:58,922
they've filed this bogus case
claiming my clients attacked them.

206
00:12:00,214 --> 00:12:01,162
Is there any evidence?

207
00:12:02,089 --> 00:12:05,463
I need to examine the Investigating Officer
of this case, Mr. Damodaran.

208
00:12:05,464 --> 00:12:06,028
Proceed.

209
00:12:08,297 --> 00:12:10,380
- You were the IO for this case, right?
- Yes, Madam.

210
00:12:10,381 --> 00:12:12,546
Did you personally inspect
the crime scene?

211
00:12:12,547 --> 00:12:14,589
Yes, Madam.
It was my duty to be there.

212
00:12:14,797 --> 00:12:15,796
What did you see there?

213
00:12:15,797 --> 00:12:19,422
Those four men... They were
writhing in pain from the beating.

214
00:12:19,589 --> 00:12:20,589
I see. And what else?

215
00:12:21,297 --> 00:12:22,671
The factory was a mess.

216
00:12:22,672 --> 00:12:23,713
Anything else?

217
00:12:23,714 --> 00:12:25,855
There were crushed biscuits
scattered everywhere, Ma'am.

218
00:12:26,256 --> 00:12:28,046
Oh. Those crushed biscuits...

219
00:12:28,047 --> 00:12:29,339
Were they butter biscuits?

220
00:12:29,464 --> 00:12:30,547
Or coconut biscuits?

221
00:12:32,214 --> 00:12:33,213
What is this, Madam?

222
00:12:33,214 --> 00:12:33,926
Silence.

223
00:12:34,672 --> 00:12:35,838
What sort of question is that?

224
00:12:35,839 --> 00:12:38,088
No, My Lord. For this case,
that detail is crucial.

225
00:12:38,089 --> 00:12:40,921
He himself said he visited the scene
and handled the investigation.

226
00:12:40,922 --> 00:12:43,046
If he had really gone there...
he should have collected

227
00:12:43,047 --> 00:12:45,671
all the physical evidence,
including broken bottles and biscuits,

228
00:12:45,672 --> 00:12:47,671
and produced it before this
court along with the seizure record.

229
00:12:47,672 --> 00:12:49,588
But no such evidence
was ever produced,

230
00:12:49,589 --> 00:12:51,214
which means he never went there.

231
00:12:51,506 --> 00:12:53,218
Don't you know you have
to produce a seizure record?

232
00:12:53,589 --> 00:12:54,839
And you call yourself a cop?

233
00:12:55,047 --> 00:12:56,047
Any cross-questions?

234
00:12:56,881 --> 00:12:57,582
Baby Kannan!

235
00:13:00,047 --> 00:13:01,172
No questions, My Lord.

236
00:13:02,089 --> 00:13:03,171
Witness dismissed.

237
00:13:03,172 --> 00:13:06,297
I need to cross-examine the complainants,
Mr. Stone and his brothers, My Lord.

238
00:13:06,422 --> 00:13:07,067
Proceed.

239
00:13:08,672 --> 00:13:10,213
- Your names?
- Stone.

240
00:13:10,214 --> 00:13:11,589
- Cold.
- Steve.

241
00:13:12,047 --> 00:13:13,047
Austin.

242
00:13:13,589 --> 00:13:16,296
We're big fans of WWE.

243
00:13:16,297 --> 00:13:18,880
That's why we got our names
legally changed.

244
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:19,963
What happened to your hand?

245
00:13:19,964 --> 00:13:21,838
The medical report has already
been submitted for that...

246
00:13:21,839 --> 00:13:22,990
I was asking him.

247
00:13:25,006 --> 00:13:25,813
What happened to your hand?

248
00:13:26,089 --> 00:13:28,963
The doctor said I had three coracoid
fractures from the beating, Madam.

249
00:13:28,964 --> 00:13:30,005
Can you raise your arm?

250
00:13:30,006 --> 00:13:31,046
No, Madam.

251
00:13:31,047 --> 00:13:33,172
If you force yourself,
how high can you raise it?

252
00:13:33,672 --> 00:13:35,755
If I lift it any further,
the pain will kill me, Madam.

253
00:13:35,756 --> 00:13:37,588
Before this happened,
what was your arm like?

254
00:13:37,589 --> 00:13:38,671
It was perfectly normal, Madam.

255
00:13:38,672 --> 00:13:39,921
So you could raise it
properly then?

256
00:13:39,922 --> 00:13:41,005
Yes, Madam.

257
00:13:41,006 --> 00:13:42,130
How high could you raise it?

258
00:13:42,131 --> 00:13:43,421
This high... all the way
up like this, Madam.

259
00:13:43,422 --> 00:13:44,589
That's enough.

260
00:13:44,839 --> 00:13:45,839
Superb!

261
00:13:48,006 --> 00:13:49,089
Silence.

262
00:13:49,672 --> 00:13:51,631
So, this is clearly
a put-up case.

263
00:13:51,797 --> 00:13:52,797
That's all, My Lord.

264
00:13:53,172 --> 00:13:54,756
Baby Kannan, any cross?

265
00:13:58,006 --> 00:14:01,088
♪ This is our territory, if our fury takes flight,
You will meet your grave tonight ♪

266
00:14:01,089 --> 00:14:04,131
♪ Non-stop blows if caught in our track,
We are built different, watch your back ♪

267
00:14:07,006 --> 00:14:09,714
Baby Kannan, any closing arguments,
or shall I issue the order?

268
00:14:09,839 --> 00:14:12,128
I have submitted all my arguments
in a written statement

269
00:14:12,381 --> 00:14:14,547
to you and the opposing counsel,
My Lord.

270
00:14:16,714 --> 00:14:18,964
The key points are
on page five, My Lord.

271
00:14:28,047 --> 00:14:28,800
Interesting point.

272
00:14:32,881 --> 00:14:33,880
But that's not enough.

273
00:14:33,881 --> 00:14:35,296
Any other points?

274
00:14:35,297 --> 00:14:36,964
Kindly refer to page seven, My Lord.

275
00:14:37,381 --> 00:14:39,714
I repeat, page number seven.

276
00:14:43,631 --> 00:14:45,505
But My Lord, there's nothing here!

277
00:14:45,506 --> 00:14:46,921
Your time is up, Preethi.

278
00:14:46,922 --> 00:14:48,172
Let him finish his argument.

279
00:14:48,506 --> 00:14:50,339
Baby Kannan, any more points?

280
00:14:50,464 --> 00:14:51,296
Oh no! Lordship!

281
00:14:51,297 --> 00:14:53,421
That's all. I've already submitted
everything I have.

282
00:14:53,422 --> 00:14:55,630
So, based on the facts
and the evidence produced,

283
00:14:55,631 --> 00:14:58,671
I pray that justice be rendered
to my aggrieved clients.

284
00:14:58,672 --> 00:14:59,538
That's all, My Lord.

285
00:15:02,756 --> 00:15:03,921
Mr. and Mrs. Sankaran,

286
00:15:03,922 --> 00:15:06,546
you damaged the property
of Golden Dust Biscuit Factory.

287
00:15:06,547 --> 00:15:08,422
Furthermore, the company's proprietors...

288
00:15:08,631 --> 00:15:10,839
Cold, Stone, Steve, and Austin...

289
00:15:11,006 --> 00:15:14,131
It has been officially proven that you
viciously attacked these four people.

290
00:15:15,506 --> 00:15:16,755
The accused ought
to be remanded.

291
00:15:16,756 --> 00:15:19,615
However, given their age, I am granting
bail on a personal bond of one lakh.

292
00:15:19,964 --> 00:15:21,588
Henceforth, without
the court's permission,

293
00:15:21,589 --> 00:15:23,421
they are barred from
entering the factory premises.

294
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:25,463
You have one month
to appeal this verdict.

295
00:15:25,464 --> 00:15:28,422
My Lord, there are no valid points
in his written statement.

296
00:15:29,131 --> 00:15:30,630
No evidence has been submitted.

297
00:15:30,631 --> 00:15:32,046
- Then how?
- Is my order wrong?

298
00:15:32,047 --> 00:15:34,005
Are you going to teach me
how to run this court?

299
00:15:34,006 --> 00:15:35,671
I proved it right before your eyes!

300
00:15:35,672 --> 00:15:37,130
Then why not challenge
it in appeal?

301
00:15:37,131 --> 00:15:38,255
That's what the High Court is for.

302
00:15:38,964 --> 00:15:40,588
So what, My Lord?
How is this accep--

303
00:15:40,589 --> 00:15:41,880
One more word from you...

304
00:15:41,881 --> 00:15:42,921
and I'll hold you in contempt.

305
00:15:42,922 --> 00:15:44,214
Court is adjourned for a break.

306
00:15:49,047 --> 00:15:50,297
Yaay!

307
00:15:51,297 --> 00:15:54,672
Baby sir, let's celebrate
this victory with a party!

308
00:15:55,214 --> 00:15:56,796
"How high can you
raise your hand?"

309
00:15:56,797 --> 00:15:59,921
When he said, "This high,"
I was startled for a second.

310
00:15:59,922 --> 00:16:02,505
Right from our college days,
you've always argued brilliantly.

311
00:16:02,506 --> 00:16:04,380
But the order never goes your way.

312
00:16:04,381 --> 00:16:06,838
How long will you keep
buying your way through?

313
00:16:06,839 --> 00:16:08,046
Know what your problem is?

314
00:16:08,047 --> 00:16:10,463
You argue your heart out in open court,
and when everyone claps,

315
00:16:10,464 --> 00:16:11,921
you start thinking
you're some big-shot lawyer.

316
00:16:11,922 --> 00:16:14,296
But a smart lawyer knows that
more than the argument, what matters...

317
00:16:14,297 --> 00:16:16,172
is knowing the judge
who's writing the verdict.

318
00:16:16,381 --> 00:16:17,755
How long do you plan
to keep going like this?

319
00:16:17,756 --> 00:16:19,671
One day, this place
is bound to change.

320
00:16:19,672 --> 00:16:21,255
And then we'll see
who survives here.

321
00:16:21,256 --> 00:16:22,505
This is my place.

322
00:16:22,506 --> 00:16:23,546
My court.

323
00:16:23,547 --> 00:16:24,671
Nothing is going to change.

324
00:16:24,672 --> 00:16:26,506
Even if God himself shows up,
he can't change a thing.

325
00:16:27,464 --> 00:16:28,797
And I won't let Him!

326
00:16:51,964 --> 00:16:52,963
Ah, Vasanthi Madam.

327
00:16:52,964 --> 00:16:54,963
We're near the temple
inside the court compound.

328
00:16:54,964 --> 00:16:56,796
The hearing isn't today,
but they're asking for the fee.

329
00:16:56,797 --> 00:16:58,047
They must be in real need.

330
00:17:35,172 --> 00:17:35,760
Sir.

331
00:17:36,214 --> 00:17:37,214
What temple is that?

332
00:17:38,381 --> 00:17:39,881
This God is incredibly powerful.

333
00:17:40,047 --> 00:17:42,755
He draws no line between
rich and poor, caste and creed.

334
00:17:42,756 --> 00:17:43,963
He belongs to everyone.

335
00:17:43,964 --> 00:17:45,839
Even the problems
the court can't solve...

336
00:17:46,047 --> 00:17:47,172
He will solve them at once.

337
00:17:47,756 --> 00:17:49,880
Every territory
has its guardian.

338
00:17:49,881 --> 00:17:51,880
He is the guardian deity
of this territory.

339
00:17:51,881 --> 00:17:54,714
He is not the soft kind of God
you please with a little camphor flame.

340
00:17:55,006 --> 00:17:56,743
Pray from your heart,
grind chillies and offer them,

341
00:17:57,131 --> 00:17:59,256
and this fierce God
will deliver instant justice.

342
00:18:00,797 --> 00:18:02,339
The lord of the hunt,
Vettai Karuppu!

343
00:18:25,089 --> 00:18:26,089
♪ Karuppa ♪

344
00:18:27,756 --> 00:18:29,178
Case passed on to
next month 17th.

345
00:18:29,589 --> 00:18:31,339
- Thank you, Your Honour.
- Next!

346
00:18:34,214 --> 00:18:36,005
Why are you taking up
return of property cases?

347
00:18:36,006 --> 00:18:37,838
Baby sir, it's 45 sovereigns.

348
00:18:37,839 --> 00:18:39,505
He's not from our state.
He doesn't know the ropes.

349
00:18:39,506 --> 00:18:40,643
What if we charge
10K per hearing?

350
00:18:44,839 --> 00:18:47,297
Return of Property,
Mattancherry Sukumaran.

351
00:18:48,089 --> 00:18:49,546
Lordship, the gold stolen
from my client--

352
00:18:49,547 --> 00:18:51,464
No one from the police station
has appeared, Your Honour.

353
00:18:52,714 --> 00:18:54,631
The case is posted to
the second of next month.

354
00:18:55,464 --> 00:18:56,123
Lordship...

355
00:18:57,381 --> 00:18:59,005
My client is an elderly man,
he's not keeping well.

356
00:18:59,006 --> 00:19:00,838
An earlier date
would really help.

357
00:19:00,839 --> 00:19:01,922
Not me!

358
00:19:02,256 --> 00:19:03,025
It's my daughter who's unwell.

359
00:19:12,047 --> 00:19:13,421
Is the 21st of this month okay?

360
00:19:13,422 --> 00:19:14,796
21st is okay, My Lord.

361
00:19:14,797 --> 00:19:15,592
Next?

362
00:19:15,922 --> 00:19:17,421
CC 4345,

363
00:19:17,422 --> 00:19:18,839
Deva versus Simon.

364
00:19:34,381 --> 00:19:35,588
- Hey, Raja.
- Sir?

365
00:19:35,589 --> 00:19:37,546
Two biryanis and two meatball sets.
Pack them to go.

366
00:19:37,547 --> 00:19:38,880
- Okay, sir.
- Make sure there's a leg piece.

367
00:19:38,881 --> 00:19:40,296
Pack one extra biryani
to go as well.

368
00:19:40,297 --> 00:19:41,671
Just give the total bill
to that girl.

369
00:19:41,672 --> 00:19:42,491
Okay, Madam.

370
00:19:42,839 --> 00:19:44,047
Why are you eating dosa?

371
00:19:44,256 --> 00:19:45,672
The biryani here is incredible.

372
00:19:46,672 --> 00:19:48,214
Yeah, I can see that.
I don't want any.

373
00:19:49,506 --> 00:19:51,213
- Baby Sir, what are you doing here?
- Hey, Meiyappan!

374
00:19:51,214 --> 00:19:53,755
I thought you only ate at five-star
hotels. And you're eating here?

375
00:19:53,756 --> 00:19:54,421
Client!

376
00:19:54,422 --> 00:19:56,603
This man's a legend in the
High Court and the Supreme Court.

377
00:19:57,006 --> 00:19:58,839
You're lucky
he's appeared in this court.

378
00:20:00,172 --> 00:20:01,630
That Biscuit Factory case of yours...

379
00:20:01,631 --> 00:20:03,596
To this day, I use that as a
masterclass for my juniors.

380
00:20:04,131 --> 00:20:05,130
Hats off, sir!

381
00:20:05,131 --> 00:20:06,380
Which master's class, sir?

382
00:20:06,381 --> 00:20:08,111
Idiot...
He said masterclass, not master's class.

383
00:20:08,656 --> 00:20:09,631
Hey, 'Ghost'!

384
00:20:10,047 --> 00:20:11,338
I've ordered some food to go.

385
00:20:11,339 --> 00:20:12,796
Collect it
and keep it in the car.

386
00:20:12,797 --> 00:20:13,880
Yes, sir.

387
00:20:13,881 --> 00:20:15,381
- Madam.
- Yes?

388
00:20:15,922 --> 00:20:17,505
You said everything
would be over today.

389
00:20:17,506 --> 00:20:19,006
Sir, we had everything ready.

390
00:20:19,172 --> 00:20:20,838
We even went to the station
and spoke to them yesterday.

391
00:20:20,839 --> 00:20:22,171
Sir, we did speak to them,
didn't we?

392
00:20:22,172 --> 00:20:24,297
Until I say so, don't come
anywhere near the court.

393
00:20:25,381 --> 00:20:26,922
The girl isn't well, Madam.

394
00:20:29,756 --> 00:20:31,171
Well, who exactly
is in perfect health?

395
00:20:31,172 --> 00:20:32,589
We begged them to come.

396
00:20:34,172 --> 00:20:34,707
Binu?

397
00:20:35,547 --> 00:20:36,964
Have you transferred the fee yet?

398
00:20:37,256 --> 00:20:38,339
No.

399
00:20:38,631 --> 00:20:39,796
Could you please do it now?

400
00:20:39,797 --> 00:20:40,398
Okay.

401
00:20:41,339 --> 00:20:42,018
I will.

402
00:20:45,797 --> 00:20:47,796
Sir, at the station,
the police told us

403
00:20:47,797 --> 00:20:49,714
the coin necklace
and chain were missing.

404
00:20:50,006 --> 00:20:51,588
Now the matter is being delayed
in court too.

405
00:20:51,589 --> 00:20:53,213
It's starting to scare me.

406
00:20:53,214 --> 00:20:54,338
I don't get you.

407
00:20:54,339 --> 00:20:55,380
A coin necklace...

408
00:20:55,381 --> 00:20:58,089
At the station, they said only
45 sovereigns were recovered,

409
00:20:58,256 --> 00:21:00,313
out of the 60 sovereigns
that were stolen.

410
00:21:01,006 --> 00:21:02,344
You should've told me
this first!

411
00:21:03,089 --> 00:21:03,694
Huh?

412
00:21:04,881 --> 00:21:05,881
Call the station.

413
00:21:06,631 --> 00:21:08,297
Never trust a cop, sir.

414
00:21:08,589 --> 00:21:09,432
Trust anyone but a cop.

415
00:21:12,006 --> 00:21:12,796
Kumaran Anna...

416
00:21:12,797 --> 00:21:15,088
- Yes, Baby sir?
- Get Inspector Jana on the line.

417
00:21:15,089 --> 00:21:17,088
He's not here now, sir.
A new lady officer is in charge.

418
00:21:17,089 --> 00:21:18,380
I don't care who it is.
Get her on the line, brother!

419
00:21:18,381 --> 00:21:19,255
- Madam...
- Who is it?

420
00:21:19,256 --> 00:21:21,338
- He's on the line, Madam. Speak.
- Who is it?

421
00:21:21,339 --> 00:21:22,381
- Hello!
- Madam!

422
00:21:22,547 --> 00:21:24,755
I'm an advocate calling
from the Seven Wells Court,

423
00:21:24,756 --> 00:21:26,439
regarding the father-daughter
jewellery theft case.

424
00:21:26,756 --> 00:21:29,296
Out of the 60 sovereigns,
15 were never accounted for. Is that right?

425
00:21:29,297 --> 00:21:30,756
Whatever is in the FIR is final.

426
00:21:31,047 --> 00:21:32,838
And I am under no obligation
to explain anything to you.

427
00:21:32,839 --> 00:21:34,838
Ma'am, the FIR itself shows
15 sovereigns less--

428
00:21:34,839 --> 00:21:36,047
Who the hell are you,
first of all?

429
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:40,922
Whoever you are,
come here in person and talk.

430
00:21:54,339 --> 00:21:55,134
Where's Gowri?

431
00:21:59,839 --> 00:22:01,546
Hey! Hey!
I got here first!

432
00:22:01,547 --> 00:22:02,922
Hey! Shut your mouth!

433
00:22:03,506 --> 00:22:04,087
Hello!

434
00:22:04,797 --> 00:22:05,300
Hello!

435
00:22:08,339 --> 00:22:08,883
Hello!

436
00:22:20,756 --> 00:22:22,672
Thanga Meena! Thanga Meena!

437
00:22:22,839 --> 00:22:24,171
Thanga Meena, the gold thief!

438
00:22:24,172 --> 00:22:26,255
Sir, you need to see this
to know what we're dealing with.

439
00:22:26,256 --> 00:22:28,506
- Don't keep pushing us.
- Okay, sir.

440
00:22:29,714 --> 00:22:31,630
Hey! What's the issue?
What the hell is going on here?

441
00:22:31,631 --> 00:22:33,546
Madam got into an argument with
a lawyer from Seven Wells court.

442
00:22:33,547 --> 00:22:34,796
- Where is Madam?
- She's inside, sir.

443
00:22:34,797 --> 00:22:36,797
Hello! Why are all of you
gathered here?

444
00:22:37,047 --> 00:22:38,880
According to the rules, I'm not
allowed to speak to the media.

445
00:22:38,881 --> 00:22:41,421
The rules also say you shouldn't
take bribes. But you do, right?

446
00:22:41,422 --> 00:22:42,755
When it comes to bribes,

447
00:22:42,756 --> 00:22:45,046
they say your station is ranked first
in all of Tamil Nadu.

448
00:22:45,047 --> 00:22:46,755
Go say that to K3 station.

449
00:22:46,756 --> 00:22:48,630
They're the ones claiming
they're number one.

450
00:22:48,631 --> 00:22:51,463
Word is, Silverwoods is giving you
a Silver Icon Award for corruption?

451
00:22:51,464 --> 00:22:52,963
Who is it they don't
give awards to?

452
00:22:52,964 --> 00:22:54,421
Just because you're the press,
you think you can ask anything?

453
00:22:54,422 --> 00:22:56,006
Who told you to do all this?

454
00:22:56,297 --> 00:22:58,047
- Thanga Meena! Thanga Meena!

455
00:22:59,839 --> 00:23:01,256
What do you want, sir?

456
00:23:01,672 --> 00:23:03,282
You recovered 60 sovereigns.

457
00:23:04,672 --> 00:23:06,672
But the FIR shows only 45.

458
00:23:07,006 --> 00:23:08,755
You think a thief would just
hand it back like that?

459
00:23:08,756 --> 00:23:10,088
That same night, they took it--

460
00:23:10,089 --> 00:23:12,213
And blew it, having a grand
time in Mahabalipuram.

461
00:23:12,214 --> 00:23:13,296
Right, Kumaran Anna?

462
00:23:13,297 --> 00:23:14,464
Correct, sir.

463
00:23:14,839 --> 00:23:18,009
My team and I are the ones who trained your
station how to cook these FIRs, Madam.

464
00:23:21,297 --> 00:23:22,297
- Kumaran Anna.
- Sir.

465
00:23:22,714 --> 00:23:24,421
- The gold is in the cupboard, right?
- Yes.

466
00:23:24,422 --> 00:23:25,506
Go get it, Anna.

467
00:23:27,006 --> 00:23:28,756
Go ahead, Anna.
Madam won't say a word.

468
00:23:30,131 --> 00:23:31,214
Okay, Madam.

469
00:23:31,339 --> 00:23:33,255
Please, just take your
people and go, sir.

470
00:23:33,256 --> 00:23:34,338
Oh, I'll leave, Madam.

471
00:23:34,339 --> 00:23:35,721
My client will be happy
once the gold is returned.

472
00:23:36,464 --> 00:23:38,339
- But my team is still outside!
- So what?

473
00:23:38,464 --> 00:23:40,086
You should have shown
some respect over the phone.

474
00:23:41,006 --> 00:23:43,464
Look! They've taken control
of your entire station.

475
00:23:43,964 --> 00:23:45,839
Trigger them, and they'll be
protesting at Marina Beach next!

476
00:23:47,964 --> 00:23:49,046
- Kumaran sir.
- Madam.

477
00:23:49,047 --> 00:23:50,464
Bring the money from the spa.

478
00:23:50,714 --> 00:23:52,213
That too?
Okay, Madam.

479
00:23:52,214 --> 00:23:54,881
Please, just take everyone
and leave, sir. Please.

480
00:23:55,756 --> 00:23:56,797
Here you go, sir.

481
00:23:57,964 --> 00:23:58,682
Okay, Madam.

482
00:23:59,381 --> 00:24:00,188
I'll give you my card.

483
00:24:00,589 --> 00:24:02,172
Call me.
We'll stay in touch.

484
00:24:03,881 --> 00:24:05,046
He's a top-tier advocate, Madam.

485
00:24:05,047 --> 00:24:06,881
Tell them Kumaran sir from the station
gave you the lead.

486
00:24:07,464 --> 00:24:09,130
Oops, sorry, Madam.
Just slipped out... force of habit.

487
00:24:09,131 --> 00:24:10,964
Thanga Meena, Thanga Meena!

488
00:24:11,506 --> 00:24:13,589
Gold Thief, Thanga Meena!

489
00:24:13,756 --> 00:24:15,588
[sloganeering continues]

490
00:24:15,589 --> 00:24:16,441
- Sir.
- Yes?

491
00:24:18,131 --> 00:24:19,381
The police didn't take it, sir.

492
00:24:19,797 --> 00:24:21,091
Those boys already sold it off.

493
00:24:21,381 --> 00:24:24,006
But the Commissioner's office
kept calling her over and over.

494
00:24:24,131 --> 00:24:25,050
She was frightened.

495
00:24:25,464 --> 00:24:28,131
Since she couldn't recover the gold,
she suggested a compromise.

496
00:24:28,297 --> 00:24:29,664
This is the bribe
she collected from a spa.

497
00:24:30,589 --> 00:24:33,005
She begged me, "Please take this
and sort this somehow."

498
00:24:33,006 --> 00:24:35,283
Now, as an honest lawyer,
I'm not supposed to touch this money.

499
00:24:36,922 --> 00:24:38,631
But if it's for the good of my client...

500
00:24:39,381 --> 00:24:40,212
I can take it, can't I, sir?

501
00:24:40,922 --> 00:24:42,094
Huh? Isn't that my duty?

502
00:24:42,756 --> 00:24:43,252
So, I took it, sir.

503
00:24:43,881 --> 00:24:45,168
Not for myself, but for you.

504
00:24:47,672 --> 00:24:49,131
I've done whatever
little I could.

505
00:24:50,464 --> 00:24:52,256
Thanga Meena, Thanga Meena!

506
00:24:52,422 --> 00:24:54,255
Gold Thief, Thanga Meena!

507
00:24:54,256 --> 00:24:56,339
Thanga Meena, Thanga Meena!

508
00:24:58,672 --> 00:25:00,213
I was just telling Binu...

509
00:25:00,214 --> 00:25:02,156
So many people went out of their way
to come here for us.

510
00:25:02,547 --> 00:25:04,005
Shouldn't we do something
in return?

511
00:25:04,006 --> 00:25:04,675
We really should.

512
00:25:06,172 --> 00:25:07,489
But for an honest lawyer...

513
00:25:08,256 --> 00:25:09,601
What has this society
ever actually given back?

514
00:25:10,047 --> 00:25:11,464
Nothing but a life of poverty.

515
00:25:17,381 --> 00:25:19,464
What if we just hand this money
out to everyone?

516
00:25:19,589 --> 00:25:20,589
Hmm?

517
00:25:21,214 --> 00:25:22,485
It's not even ours
to begin with, right?

518
00:25:23,172 --> 00:25:24,271
- It's bribe money.
- Hmm.

519
00:25:24,589 --> 00:25:25,881
So? Is it okay with you?

520
00:25:27,672 --> 00:25:28,684
Are you okay with it, dear?

521
00:25:31,797 --> 00:25:32,372
Give it to them.

522
00:25:34,422 --> 00:25:35,300
- Sir.
- Yes?

523
00:25:35,922 --> 00:25:37,031
For a man with a heart
as big as yours...

524
00:25:37,714 --> 00:25:38,963
Everything is bound to turn out well.

525
00:25:38,964 --> 00:25:40,381
God will protect
a good man like you.

526
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:53,380
♪ La justice n'est pa la ♪

527
00:25:53,381 --> 00:25:56,755
♪ A toute a l'heure ♪
♪ A toute a l'heure ♪

528
