Baby sir said that
we'll get our gold tomorrow.

599
00:29:37,297 --> 00:29:38,796
We'll collect it from the court,

600
00:29:38,797 --> 00:29:40,088
go straight to the hospital,

601
00:29:40,089 --> 00:29:42,297
then it's observation,
with the surgery the day after.

602
00:29:46,922 --> 00:29:49,964
Do you know that Mohanlal and
Dulquer Salmaan have houses in Chennai?

603
00:29:50,422 --> 00:29:51,084
Shall we go and see them?

604
00:29:52,506 --> 00:29:53,930
Once the surgery is over
and we're discharged...

605
00:29:54,339 --> 00:29:56,256
we'll go see their houses
before heading back.

606
00:29:58,006 --> 00:29:59,797
Check what the gold price is today.

607
00:30:00,589 --> 00:30:01,964
- Just check it!
- Dad!!

608
00:30:03,547 --> 00:30:04,964
We're never getting our gold back!

609
00:30:06,589 --> 00:30:07,762
Don't you get it?

610
00:30:08,131 --> 00:30:09,297
They're scamming us!

611
00:30:10,339 --> 00:30:12,780
If they actually recover the gold,
they can't keep milking us for money.

612
00:30:13,089 --> 00:30:14,422
All they care about is G-Pay!

613
00:30:15,214 --> 00:30:16,214
Look, Dad!

614
00:30:16,381 --> 00:30:17,031
Look!!!

615
00:30:17,506 --> 00:30:19,672
Biryani! Biryani!
Biryani! Biryani!

616
00:30:20,756 --> 00:30:22,963
Ice cream, Cigarettes, Beeda.

617
00:30:22,964 --> 00:30:23,906
The list is endless!

618
00:30:24,631 --> 00:30:27,131
I can't stand seeing you
humiliate yourself for them anymore.

619
00:30:27,422 --> 00:30:28,631
Let's just go home.

620
00:30:29,381 --> 00:30:31,089
I can't bear to see you like this.

621
00:30:31,881 --> 00:30:33,839
I'm done!
I can't deal with these people anymore!

622
00:30:35,297 --> 00:30:36,330
- Let's go.
- Cry!

623
00:30:37,256 --> 00:30:38,297
Cry!

624
00:30:38,881 --> 00:30:40,464
Cry your heart out if you have to.

625
00:30:42,047 --> 00:30:43,172
But I'm not going to cry.

626
00:30:44,214 --> 00:30:45,214
I just know it!

627
00:30:45,547 --> 00:30:46,881
We're getting our gold tomorrow.

628
00:30:47,506 --> 00:30:49,047
Then we head straight to the hospital.

629
00:30:49,631 --> 00:30:52,017
And the surgery will be a success.

630
00:30:52,422 --> 00:30:53,631
I'm certain of it!

631
00:30:53,964 --> 00:30:54,463
That's why!

632
00:30:55,172 --> 00:30:56,797
Do you know how
I can be so sure?

633
00:30:58,006 --> 00:30:58,480
Ask me!

634
00:30:59,089 --> 00:31:00,171
- Ask me!
- How?

635
00:31:00,172 --> 00:31:01,546
Look me in the eye and ask me!

636
00:31:02,881 --> 00:31:04,463
Ask me how, dear!

637
00:31:04,464 --> 00:31:04,993
How?

638
00:31:06,506 --> 00:31:08,172
"Once I've made a decision...

639
00:31:08,381 --> 00:31:09,839
I don't even listen to myself!"

640
00:31:11,006 --> 00:31:12,089
Get it?

641
00:31:12,339 --> 00:31:13,179
Remember that?

642
00:31:13,464 --> 00:31:14,631
It's from 'Pokkiri'!

643
00:31:15,464 --> 00:31:16,881
Your favourite actor
Vijay's movie!

644
00:31:19,047 --> 00:31:20,380
Now lie down and get some sleep.

645
00:31:20,381 --> 00:31:20,906
Lie down!

646
00:31:21,881 --> 00:31:24,881
You don't have to come tomorrow.
I'll go to court and get it myself, okay?

647
00:31:48,422 --> 00:31:51,088
Return of Property,
Mattancherry Sukumaran.

648
00:31:51,089 --> 00:31:53,213
Lordship, all the documents
have been produced today.

649
00:31:53,214 --> 00:31:54,474
The officer is also present in court.

650
00:31:55,339 --> 00:31:57,922
Hey! Where were you all this while?
You didn't show up even once.

651
00:31:58,131 --> 00:32:00,255
Sir, I was away
investigating a case.

652
00:32:00,256 --> 00:32:02,528
As if you're Sherlock Holmes
out there solving some grand mystery!

653
00:32:05,631 --> 00:32:07,463
- Have you filed the report?
- I have, sir.

654
00:32:07,464 --> 00:32:09,255
- Appraiser?
- Greetings, sir.

655
00:32:09,256 --> 00:32:10,796
How is everyone actually here today?
It's a miracle.

656
00:32:10,797 --> 00:32:12,104
At this rate, it might
actually rain today!

657
00:32:14,464 --> 00:32:15,463
Did you check it?

658
00:32:15,464 --> 00:32:17,506
Yes, sir.
I am submitting it now.

659
00:32:26,964 --> 00:32:28,006
Sir!

660
00:32:29,964 --> 00:32:31,172
The court is adjourned.

661
00:32:32,672 --> 00:32:34,296
His Lordship is leaving
on an emergency.

662
00:32:34,297 --> 00:32:36,381
All the cases listed today
will be posted to another date.

663
00:32:37,006 --> 00:32:39,131
Sir, please! Give me my
jewellery before you go.

664
00:32:39,256 --> 00:32:40,881
Where are you going now, sir?

665
00:32:41,172 --> 00:32:42,713
Everyone is actually here today, sir!

666
00:32:42,714 --> 00:32:45,255
Sir, go wherever you need to,
but please give me my gold first.

667
00:32:45,256 --> 00:32:47,088
I've been running from pillar to post
for four months, sir!

668
00:32:47,089 --> 00:32:49,422
The gold is right in front of you!
Just give it to me before you leave.

669
00:32:50,089 --> 00:32:52,005
- Sir, I promised my daughter.
- Please don't shout, sir.

670
00:32:52,006 --> 00:32:53,213
I have to give it to her today.

671
00:32:53,214 --> 00:32:54,713
How can you just walk away like this?

672
00:32:54,714 --> 00:32:56,255
Just get my gold and give it to me!

673
00:32:56,256 --> 00:32:59,047
You can't shout in court like this.
You'll only provoke the judge!

674
00:33:00,131 --> 00:33:01,505
Hey, tell Baby Kannan
to come to my chamber!

675
00:33:01,506 --> 00:33:04,296
We got it back from the thieves,
but I can't get it back from them!

676
00:33:04,297 --> 00:33:06,421
- I need my gold. Get it for me, sir!
- Chetta, come!

677
00:33:06,422 --> 00:33:07,713
Sir, how can you shout
like that in court?

678
00:33:07,714 --> 00:33:09,130
He let you off only because
you're Baby sir's client.

679
00:33:09,131 --> 00:33:10,463
Anyone else would have been
thrown in a cell by now!

680
00:33:10,464 --> 00:33:11,796
A judge may leave
for a hundred different reasons.

681
00:33:11,797 --> 00:33:14,171
It could be a dying declaration
or a family emergency...

682
00:33:14,172 --> 00:33:15,588
He doesn't owe you
an explanation for everything!

683
00:33:15,589 --> 00:33:16,880
A judge is like God.

684
00:33:16,881 --> 00:33:18,296
Don't question them.
Just fold your hands and pray!

685
00:33:18,297 --> 00:33:19,422
Have you lost your mind?

686
00:33:20,089 --> 00:33:20,849
You think you're some big shot?

687
00:33:21,506 --> 00:33:22,686
Is that how you talk to a judge?

688
00:33:22,922 --> 00:33:24,088
This might be
the only case you have.

689
00:33:24,089 --> 00:33:25,588
But I deal with a thousand like it
every single day!

690
00:33:25,589 --> 00:33:28,213
And you won't settle a single one
of those thousand cases, sir!

691
00:33:28,214 --> 00:33:30,671
You're too busy begging for G-Pay
and stuffing your face with biryani!

692
00:33:30,672 --> 00:33:32,339
- I'll find some other good--
- How dare you point fingers at him!

693
00:33:35,172 --> 00:33:37,338
The judge called me to his chamber
and gave me an earful.

694
00:33:37,339 --> 00:33:38,150
Lunatic!

695
00:33:38,547 --> 00:33:40,422
Let's see who helps you
get your gold back now!

696
00:33:48,172 --> 00:33:48,419
Sir!

697
00:33:50,964 --> 00:33:51,579
Here, have this, sir.

698
00:33:54,381 --> 00:33:55,631
I'm just like you, sir.

699
00:33:56,714 --> 00:33:58,017
I too came here to fight a case once.

700
00:33:58,339 --> 00:33:59,081
Hard to believe, isn't it?

701
00:33:59,547 --> 00:34:00,554
That was thirty years ago.

702
00:34:01,881 --> 00:34:03,839
When I came here,
I was your daughter's age.

703
00:34:05,589 --> 00:34:07,464
My entire family
was killed in an accident.

704
00:34:07,672 --> 00:34:10,006
Claiming that I had died with them,
our local legislator...

705
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:12,464
issued a death certificate
and usurped all my property.

706
00:34:13,422 --> 00:34:14,964
"No, I didn't die,"

707
00:34:15,339 --> 00:34:16,339
"I'm still alive,"

708
00:34:16,839 --> 00:34:18,796
I came here to fight a case
just to prove that, sir.

709
00:34:18,797 --> 00:34:21,172
Until these people
bled me dry of my last penny...

710
00:34:21,464 --> 00:34:23,256
I fought that case.
For seventeen years!

711
00:34:24,339 --> 00:34:26,571
After that, I couldn't go on.
No money... and no one to turn to.

712
00:34:29,631 --> 00:34:31,380
Since then, I just do
whatever odd jobs they give me.

713
00:34:31,381 --> 00:34:33,046
I take whatever
little money they throw my way.

714
00:34:33,047 --> 00:34:35,214
I wear their old, discarded clothes...

715
00:34:35,839 --> 00:34:37,380
and have grown used
to staying here.

716
00:34:37,381 --> 00:34:39,130
I can't go out
and find work anywhere else.

717
00:34:39,131 --> 00:34:40,381
Because on paper... I'm dead.

718
00:34:40,964 --> 00:34:42,130
That's why they call me “Ghost.”

719
00:34:42,131 --> 00:34:43,010
That's my name now, sir.

720
00:34:43,881 --> 00:34:45,893
It's been so long,
I've even forgotten my real name.

721
00:34:48,506 --> 00:34:51,381
People think that if they come to court,
punishment will be handed out.

722
00:34:53,756 --> 00:34:55,797
But coming to court
is a punishment in itself, sir.

723
00:35:01,006 --> 00:35:01,758
Have it, sir.

724
00:35:02,589 --> 00:35:04,671
You need a lot of strength
to fight a case here.

725
00:35:04,672 --> 00:35:05,672
Please eat.

726
00:35:21,631 --> 00:35:23,214
This God is incredibly powerful, sir.

727
00:35:23,547 --> 00:35:25,422
Even the problems
the court cannot solve...

728
00:35:25,714 --> 00:35:27,089
He will solve them at once.

729
00:35:37,256 --> 00:35:39,338
Pray from your heart,
grind chillies and offer them,

730
00:35:39,339 --> 00:35:41,506
and this fierce God
will deliver instant justice.

731
00:36:26,297 --> 00:36:28,464
Let's see who helps you
get your gold back now!

732
00:36:30,589 --> 00:36:54,338
♪ Lord Karuppa, manifest thy power ♪

733
00:36:54,339 --> 00:36:57,089
Lord Karuppa!

734
00:37:09,422 --> 00:37:12,422
Baby sir, I promised to throw a party
if we win the case, didn't I?

735
00:37:14,922 --> 00:37:16,171
Bro, pop this!

736
00:37:16,172 --> 00:37:17,796
- You'll see God Himself!
- Hey, one is enough!

737
00:37:17,797 --> 00:37:20,796
♪ We are four, standing tall,
With no fear of the fall ♪

738
00:37:20,797 --> 00:37:24,130
♪ This ring is our spider web, our snare,
You'll find no escape in there ♪

739
00:37:24,131 --> 00:37:27,421
♪ No matter who the referee may be,
The rules will remain a mystery ♪

740
00:37:27,422 --> 00:37:30,380
♪ Bring your backup, bring your crew,
This fight won't end until we're through ♪

741
00:37:30,381 --> 00:37:32,506
♪ We are four, standing tall ♪

742
00:37:33,756 --> 00:37:35,714
♪ This ring is our spider web ♪

743
00:37:36,672 --> 00:37:42,338
♪ No matter who the referee may be ♪

744
00:37:42,339 --> 00:37:45,630
Baby sir, no one can beat you!

745
00:37:45,631 --> 00:37:46,672
You're the King!

746
00:38:06,422 --> 00:38:07,422
Hey!

747
00:38:07,714 --> 00:38:08,839
Go check, man!

748
00:38:28,422 --> 00:38:29,631
What's happening?

749
00:39:44,464 --> 00:39:46,714
♪ This is God mode ♪

750
00:39:47,881 --> 00:39:50,047
♪ This is God mode ♪

751
00:39:51,214 --> 00:39:53,171
♪ This is God Mode ♪

752
00:39:53,172 --> 00:39:55,046
♪ The sound will forever explode ♪

753
00:39:55,047 --> 00:40:03,714
♪ The shores blaze bright, masses unite,
Scream my name in roaring might ♪

754
00:40:28,506 --> 00:40:29,756
Blast!

755
00:41:16,547 --> 00:41:17,649
Wow!

756
00:41:18,547 --> 00:41:20,756
♪ This is God mode ♪

757
00:41:22,089 --> 00:41:24,256
♪ This is God mode ♪

758
00:41:25,547 --> 00:41:27,463
♪ This is God Mode ♪

759
00:41:27,464 --> 00:41:29,296
♪ The sound will forever explode ♪

760
00:41:29,297 --> 00:41:38,131
♪ The shores blaze bright, masses unite,
Scream my name in roaring might ♪

761
00:42:15,464 --> 00:42:16,091
Man, what a pill!

762
00:42:17,256 --> 00:42:18,631
The high isn't
slowing down at all!

763
00:42:18,881 --> 00:42:20,339
It's only just hitting the peak!

764
00:42:22,047 --> 00:42:23,380
Which player are you?

765
00:42:23,381 --> 00:42:24,631
The Great Khali?

766
00:42:25,089 --> 00:42:27,506
Silent type, huh?
Fine, I'm out of here.

767
00:42:27,881 --> 00:42:29,381
My name is Karuppu!

768
00:42:30,839 --> 00:42:31,727
Vettai Karuppu!

769
00:42:33,631 --> 00:42:34,724
Oh, is that so?
Then I'm Shivan...

770
00:42:35,547 --> 00:42:36,623
Vignesh Shivan.

771
00:42:37,422 --> 00:42:41,630
♪ Rathamaaran Mothamaaran ♪

772
00:42:41,631 --> 00:42:46,964
♪ Vetrimaaran Vettai Karuppa! ♪

773
00:43:05,047 --> 00:43:05,809
Oh no! Ghosts!

774
00:43:06,297 --> 00:43:08,089
Oh God! Let go of me!

775
00:43:08,922 --> 00:43:11,339
Wait! I didn't mean it
literally, God!

776
00:43:21,131 --> 00:43:22,672
Oh! God! Saamy!

777
00:43:23,922 --> 00:43:25,172
Lord Vettai Karuppu Saamy!

778
00:43:28,131 --> 00:43:29,546
Why have You appeared before me?

779
00:43:29,547 --> 00:43:31,507
Today is the day
you pay for your sins.

780
00:43:31,881 --> 00:43:33,172
What did I even do wrong?

781
00:43:33,506 --> 00:43:34,672
Do you really want to see?

782
00:43:45,089 --> 00:43:46,566
O Lord! Forgive me, Lord.

783
00:43:47,172 --> 00:43:48,797
It was just a tiny mistake!

784
00:43:48,964 --> 00:43:50,881
- Tiny?
- Okay, it's big! It's huge!

785
00:43:51,506 --> 00:43:53,255
Just give me one more chance.

786
00:43:53,256 --> 00:43:55,296
I'll fix everything
by tomorrow, I swear!

787
00:43:55,297 --> 00:43:57,671
What you failed to do for months,
how will you do it in a day?

788
00:43:57,672 --> 00:43:59,338
I only held it up all these months
on purpose, Lord!

789
00:43:59,339 --> 00:44:00,713
That's the only way
I can keep taking fees.

790
00:44:00,714 --> 00:44:03,006
That's how I can afford
a watch on my left and my right, right?

791
00:44:03,506 --> 00:44:04,338
Money, Lord! Money!!!

792
00:44:04,339 --> 00:44:06,046
But this is a trivial matter for me.

793
00:44:06,047 --> 00:44:08,130
Return of property orders
can be obtained in a day.

794
00:44:08,131 --> 00:44:09,505
I just need to grease a few palms.

795
00:44:09,506 --> 00:44:12,171
The bench clerk is easy. A cycle for
his daughter should do the trick.

796
00:44:12,172 --> 00:44:13,380
Next, police report.

797
00:44:13,381 --> 00:44:15,589
Throw him 500 rupees,
and he'll show up right away.

798
00:44:15,714 --> 00:44:17,756
Then there's the appraiser
to verify the gold.

799
00:44:17,922 --> 00:44:18,796
Know an appraiser?

800
00:44:18,797 --> 00:44:21,046
A bottle of liquor
will get you that report.

801
00:44:21,047 --> 00:44:23,713
Once that's done, you head to the Judge,
but the assistant blocks your way.

802
00:44:23,714 --> 00:44:26,838
- "You can't see him."
- Slip him 200, and you're in.

803
00:44:26,839 --> 00:44:29,671
Then there's the Judge himself.
Keep him happy, and...

804
00:44:29,672 --> 00:44:31,880
- "I'll issue the order immediately."
- The job will be done tomorrow itself.

805
00:44:31,881 --> 00:44:33,130
You've got some nerve...

806
00:44:33,131 --> 00:44:35,588
Telling me to my face
you'll buy your way out of this.

807
00:44:35,589 --> 00:44:37,005
God, what do you expect?

808
00:44:37,006 --> 00:44:38,546
Nothing works in our court
unless you grease the wheels.

809
00:44:38,547 --> 00:44:40,089
If I don't set things up--

810
00:44:48,964 --> 00:44:49,964
Hello!

811
00:44:50,256 --> 00:44:52,506
You can say bribes are wrong
and corruption is a plague...

812
00:44:53,631 --> 00:44:55,881
We're used to it. We actually like it.
It's our favourite addiction.

813
00:45:05,506 --> 00:45:07,006
We have our own procedure!

814
00:45:07,256 --> 00:45:09,171
Even if God himself shows up,
He can't change it!

815
00:45:09,172 --> 00:45:11,463
Oh no, I didn't mean that!
Forgive me, God!

816
00:45:11,464 --> 00:45:12,672
Oh no! I'm burning!

817
00:45:12,881 --> 00:45:14,797
I will atone for that sin.

818
00:45:15,006 --> 00:45:17,755
We can strike a deal!
I'll do everything You like!

819
00:45:17,756 --> 00:45:20,505
I'll sacrifice a goat, serve porridge,
carry the Kavadi, I'll even host a festival!

820
00:45:20,506 --> 00:45:22,421
I'll eat off the ground
and light a flour lamp.

821
00:45:22,422 --> 00:45:24,380
I'll shave my head
and sing Your praises!

822
00:45:24,381 --> 00:45:27,505
♪ Thunder rumbles
for Lord Karuppusaamy ♪

823
00:45:27,506 --> 00:45:30,006
♪ The golden vessel gleams! ♪

824
00:45:30,214 --> 00:45:32,921
I'll do whatever you want.
Let me go, Saamy! I'm burning!

825
00:45:32,922 --> 00:45:36,296
It's a sin to punish me like this...
To take my life for no reason, God!

826
00:45:36,297 --> 00:45:38,380
This injustice will haunt You forever!

827
00:45:38,381 --> 00:45:41,214
You are the God of Justice...
how can You let justice fail?

828
00:45:47,547 --> 00:45:48,547
What did you say?

829
00:45:48,881 --> 00:45:51,256
You are the God of Justice...
how can You let justice fail?

830
00:45:52,589 --> 00:45:54,546
Our court functions
exactly the way I told You!

831
00:45:54,547 --> 00:45:56,671
Yet you're punishing me
without even knowing how things work!

832
00:45:56,672 --> 00:45:59,005
You're God, aren't You?
The Almighty God of Justice!

833
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,630
Then come... step into our court!

834
00:46:00,631 --> 00:46:01,796
If You can...

835
00:46:01,797 --> 00:46:04,088
recover that girl's gold
through honest means,

836
00:46:04,089 --> 00:46:05,755
then punish me however You like.

837
00:46:05,756 --> 00:46:07,088
I'll accept my fate then.

838
00:46:07,089 --> 00:46:08,213
Think You can do it?

839
00:46:08,214 --> 00:46:09,421
Do You accept the challenge?

840
00:46:09,422 --> 00:46:11,881
Does the God of Justice
actually have faith in justice?

841
00:46:12,131 --> 00:46:13,287
If You do, then come prove it!

842
00:46:28,422 --> 00:46:29,755
Please sign right here.

843
00:46:29,756 --> 00:46:31,463
This is just a routine case for me.

844
00:46:31,464 --> 00:46:34,005
Raja! Pack two mutton biryanis
and one meatball set.

845
00:46:34,006 --> 00:46:34,736
Quick, quick.

846
00:46:35,297 --> 00:46:37,756
- Have you signed?
- Ganesh sir, what are you doing here?

847
00:46:37,881 --> 00:46:39,838
I thought you only ate
at five-star hotels.

848
00:46:39,839 --> 00:46:42,255
This man's a legend in the
High Court and the Supreme Court.

849
00:46:42,256 --> 00:46:43,880
That Limestone Canal case of yours...

850
00:46:43,881 --> 00:46:45,588
I use it as a
masterclass for my juniors!

851
00:46:45,589 --> 00:46:46,631
Superb, sir.

852
00:46:49,506 --> 00:46:51,756
Okay, pay the bill,
including the take away.

853
00:46:52,589 --> 00:46:54,256
They are all the same, Dad.

854
00:46:54,964 --> 00:46:56,546
We can't trust a single one of them.

855
00:46:56,547 --> 00:46:58,089
We don't have any other choice, dear.

856
00:46:58,631 --> 00:47:00,213
We've got to trust someone.

857
00:47:00,214 --> 00:47:01,195
Will you trust me?

858
00:47:29,506 --> 00:47:31,256
If You have faith in justice, come!

859
00:47:31,672 --> 00:47:32,796
Do You accept the challenge?

860
00:47:32,797 --> 00:47:33,839
I'm coming!

861
00:47:34,714 --> 00:47:36,339
I'm coming to your court!

862
00:47:36,839 --> 00:47:39,130
The day I change
your court's procedures...

863
00:47:39,131 --> 00:47:40,797
will be the day
you meet your end.

864
00:47:44,839 --> 00:47:45,839
Come, Karuppu!

865
00:47:46,256 --> 00:47:49,006
Many like you have stepped in here,
dreaming of changing the system.

866
00:47:49,922 --> 00:47:50,588
Welcome.

867
00:47:51,047 --> 00:47:52,704
Nice line. You think you're
Bharathiraja from Aayitha Ezhuthu?

868
00:47:55,464 --> 00:47:57,381
[song from "Aayitha Ezhuthu"]

869
00:48:04,881 --> 00:48:05,922
Submit the petitions.

870
00:48:06,714 --> 00:48:08,131
Bring it.
Give it, give it.

871
00:48:08,756 --> 00:48:09,755
Give it, give it.

872
00:48:09,756 --> 00:48:11,130
[song distorts comically]

873
00:48:11,131 --> 00:48:13,671
[indistinct chatter]

874
00:48:13,672 --> 00:48:15,671
Hey, don't try this
shouting business with me!

875
00:48:15,672 --> 00:48:17,296
Can't you raise your own son properly?

876
00:48:17,297 --> 00:48:20,796
[indistinct arguments]

877
00:48:20,797 --> 00:48:22,088
Hey, give it.

878
00:48:22,089 --> 00:48:23,131
One by one...

879
00:48:23,422 --> 00:48:24,631
Give them one by one, man!

880
00:48:24,922 --> 00:48:26,089
Brother!

881
00:48:26,297 --> 00:48:27,464
- Hey, brother.
- Yes?

882
00:48:27,839 --> 00:48:29,547
Are you new here?

883
00:48:29,756 --> 00:48:30,838
Yes!

884
00:48:30,839 --> 00:48:33,422
Stand around like this
and you'll be standing here forever.

885
00:48:33,756 --> 00:48:35,213
Come with your Akka.

886
00:48:35,214 --> 00:48:36,255
Come with me.

887
00:48:36,256 --> 00:48:40,339
[song from "Jai Bhim"]

888
00:48:42,131 --> 00:48:43,297
Hey, move!

889
00:48:47,506 --> 00:48:49,463
- The judge will be here now. Move!
- Sir! Sir! Sir!

890
00:48:49,464 --> 00:48:51,005
- Please, sir.
- What?

891
00:48:51,006 --> 00:48:52,046
- Give it.
- Give it.

892
00:48:52,047 --> 00:48:53,088
- Go!
- Sir!

893
00:48:53,089 --> 00:48:55,380
- What? Another petition?
- Please, sir. Just accept this one.

894
00:48:55,381 --> 00:48:56,796
Go away. It's too late.
Come back tomorrow.

895
00:48:56,797 --> 00:48:58,338
He's new to the court, sir.
We should be helping him out.

896
00:48:58,339 --> 00:48:59,255
Ask him to come tomorrow.

897
00:48:59,256 --> 00:49:01,256
He's my brother, sir.

898
00:49:02,589 --> 00:49:03,589
Yes!

899
00:49:03,922 --> 00:49:04,922
Done!

900
00:49:06,714 --> 00:49:10,672
[song from "Jai Bhim"]

901
00:49:22,464 --> 00:49:23,464
Be seated.

902
00:49:25,714 --> 00:49:28,422
Return of property.
Mattancherry Sukumaran.

903
00:49:35,381 --> 00:49:36,755
By the way, who are you?

904
00:49:36,756 --> 00:49:38,130
I've never seen you
in this court before!

905
00:49:38,131 --> 00:49:39,172
My name is Saravanan.

906
00:49:39,922 --> 00:49:40,922
From the Madurai Bench.

907
00:49:41,422 --> 00:49:43,592
- My client Mattancherry--
- Your Honourship, My Lord.

908
00:49:44,422 --> 00:49:45,505
I am their lawyer.

909
00:49:45,506 --> 00:49:47,088
I have the signed petition right here!

910
00:49:47,089 --> 00:49:48,506
My Lord, Your Honour.

911
00:49:50,089 --> 00:49:52,171
Look at this, My Lord.
I have the signed petition.

912
00:49:52,172 --> 00:49:53,755
- I am their lawyer.
- What's going on here?

913
00:49:53,756 --> 00:49:55,713
Three of you are appearing
for the same case?

914
00:49:55,714 --> 00:49:56,756
Not three!

915
00:49:57,631 --> 00:49:59,796
There are four of us
in total, Your Honor.

916
00:49:59,797 --> 00:50:01,297
Selvi, you too?

917
00:50:01,506 --> 00:50:04,213
Yes, Your Honour. Look, I have
the signed petition right here.

918
00:50:04,214 --> 00:50:05,463
I am the rightful lawyer.

919
00:50:05,464 --> 00:50:08,022
How can you just believe any
random person off the street, Your Honour?

920
00:50:08,297 --> 00:50:11,338
[song distorts comically]

921
00:50:11,339 --> 00:50:12,671
Hey, whose phone is that?

922
00:50:12,672 --> 00:50:14,131
Playing random songs!
Get out!

923
00:50:15,672 --> 00:50:17,338
So, what exactly is your dispute?

924
00:50:17,339 --> 00:50:18,756
I'm the one representing them.

925
00:50:18,881 --> 00:50:20,797
- I know them personally.
- You know them?

926
00:50:21,256 --> 00:50:22,714
They are my relatives, My Lord.

927
00:50:22,964 --> 00:50:25,171
Madam, Madam, Madam!
Don't just make things up as you go!

928
00:50:25,172 --> 00:50:26,880
Your Honour, I am their lawyer.

929
00:50:26,881 --> 00:50:27,921
The signed petition is with me.

930
00:50:27,922 --> 00:50:30,796
Do you just accept petitions from anyone?
Don't you check them?

931
00:50:30,797 --> 00:50:32,088
- Sorry, sir.
- What do you mean, "sorry"?

932
00:50:32,089 --> 00:50:34,088
Only one of these four petitions
better show up on my desk tomorrow.

933
00:50:34,089 --> 00:50:36,047
Otherwise, I won't hear this case at all.
Am I clear?

934
00:50:37,922 --> 00:50:39,381
Court is adjourned for a break.

935
00:51:02,381 --> 00:51:04,088
Haven't we been your
lawyers all this time?

936
00:51:04,089 --> 00:51:06,546
How is it fair to suddenly
bring in someone else, Madam?

937
00:51:06,547 --> 00:51:08,406
You haven't appeared for
even a single hearing so far.

938
00:51:08,922 --> 00:51:11,255
You haven't produced any
of the evidence I gave you in court.

939
00:51:11,256 --> 00:51:12,296
Give me my case file.

940
00:51:12,297 --> 00:51:13,671
- I will proceed with him for this case.
- Madam!

941
00:51:13,672 --> 00:51:15,297
Is this some ordinary case?

942
00:51:16,256 --> 00:51:17,839
It's a sexual assault case.

943
00:51:18,714 --> 00:51:20,464
And that too,
against a former minister.

944
00:51:21,339 --> 00:51:24,006
Do you have any idea
who you're up against?

945
00:51:24,297 --> 00:51:25,421
Baby Kannan!

946
00:51:25,422 --> 00:51:26,921
You've got only two options.

947
00:51:26,922 --> 00:51:29,547
Either stick with us,
or withdraw the case entirely.

948
00:51:29,839 --> 00:51:30,964
Are you threatening her?

949
00:51:31,506 --> 00:51:33,172
I've seen this circus before.

950
00:51:33,339 --> 00:51:35,964
Are you taking her money
just to do Baby Kannan's dirty work?

951
00:51:38,881 --> 00:51:40,131
Are you new to the court, sir?

952
00:51:41,131 --> 00:51:42,005
Yes.

953
00:51:42,006 --> 00:51:43,526
Those three are
on the same team.

954
00:51:43,839 --> 00:51:45,493
They pull this stunt
whenever someone new turns up.

955
00:51:45,839 --> 00:51:47,296
One single complaint...

956
00:51:47,297 --> 00:51:49,296
and you'll be barred
from practising law for life.

957
00:51:49,297 --> 00:51:51,089
We aren't practising advocates.

958
00:52:08,881 --> 00:52:10,338
Can't you lot do anything properly?

959
00:52:10,339 --> 00:52:12,171
Look, there's blood
all over Madam's face.

960
00:52:12,172 --> 00:52:13,921
They can't even do a simple job neatly.
Sorry, Madam.

961
00:52:13,922 --> 00:52:15,338
Why are you shivering, sir?

962
00:52:15,339 --> 00:52:17,296
With your car in that state,
how will you get home?

963
00:52:17,297 --> 00:52:18,714
Should I have my boys
drop you off?

964
00:52:19,839 --> 00:52:20,839
Hey!

965
00:52:21,714 --> 00:52:22,797
Sir, the case file?

966
00:52:25,256 --> 00:52:26,797
- No.
- What did you say?

967
00:52:27,422 --> 00:52:29,381
A "double game"?
There's only one game being played here!

968
00:52:31,381 --> 00:52:33,179
He wasn't taking your money
to work for me on the side.

969
00:52:33,672 --> 00:52:35,503
He only came to fight your case
because I sent him!

970
00:52:36,131 --> 00:52:37,806
And it took you this long
to figure that out.

971
00:52:38,589 --> 00:52:40,194
It's nearly impossible
to fight a case in this court.

972
00:52:40,756 --> 00:52:42,339
Look... the man himself is right here.

973
00:52:43,464 --> 00:52:45,922
Just say the word,
and I'll get you a massive settlement.

974
00:52:46,381 --> 00:52:47,547
Withdraw the case.

975
00:52:47,922 --> 00:52:49,147
You think chasing
away one lawyer...

976
00:52:49,922 --> 00:52:51,381
means there's no one
else left here?

977
00:52:52,297 --> 00:52:53,964
There are a thousand
other lawyers here.

978
00:52:54,214 --> 00:52:55,464
Give me the case file.

979
00:53:10,381 --> 00:53:12,547
Those thousand lawyers
you mentioned are all here.

980
00:53:13,131 --> 00:53:15,339
If even one of them
has the guts to touch this file...

981
00:53:15,672 --> 00:53:16,922
let him fight the case.

982
00:53:18,547 --> 00:53:21,297
Once a file is wrapped in that bandana,
no one will ever take it up.

983
00:53:34,922 --> 00:53:37,171
What happened, Moorthy sir?
Not picking it up this time?

984
00:53:37,172 --> 00:53:38,172
No, Baby sir.

985
00:53:42,631 --> 00:53:44,130
The file is wrapped in the bandana.

986
00:53:44,131 --> 00:53:45,589
They won't even dare to touch it.

987
00:53:45,922 --> 00:53:48,297
Your case will never see
the inside of a courtroom.

988
00:53:53,631 --> 00:53:55,463
Half those people
aren't even real lawyers.

989
00:53:55,464 --> 00:53:57,339
They're Baby Kannan's
kangaroo court team.

990
00:53:57,506 --> 00:53:58,921
This is exactly how they operate.

991
00:53:58,922 --> 00:54:01,255
Do you know how many people
have been affected like this?

992
00:54:01,256 --> 00:54:03,963
Go to those three,
give them ₹500 or ₹1000,

993
00:54:03,964 --> 00:54:05,338
they'll withdraw their petitions.

994
00:54:05,339 --> 00:54:07,255
They aren't nearly as dangerous
as these people.

995
00:54:07,256 --> 00:54:09,256
Where can I find them now?

996
00:54:10,006 --> 00:54:10,876
They'll be in the lawyers' chamber.

997
00:54:11,756 --> 00:54:13,380
Hmmm.
Here he comes.

998
00:54:13,381 --> 00:54:16,088
Madam! Looks like we've got
a big fish on the hook today!

999
00:54:16,089 --> 00:54:16,453
Yeah!

1000
00:54:17,756 --> 00:54:19,046
Welcome, sir!

1001
00:54:19,047 --> 00:54:21,796
Madam, didn't I tell you
he'd come looking for us?

1002
00:54:21,797 --> 00:54:23,338
Please, withdraw your petitions.

1003
00:54:23,339 --> 00:54:24,922
- Withdraw?
- Sir!

1004
00:54:25,131 --> 00:54:26,838
You've landed yourself
a massive case.

1005
00:54:26,839 --> 00:54:28,297
45 sovereigns!

1006
00:54:29,006 --> 00:54:31,171
You'll be taking a huge percentage
as your fee anyway.

1007
00:54:31,172 --> 00:54:32,755
Why not give us a little share?

1008
00:54:32,756 --> 00:54:34,256
I don't take money.

1009
00:54:34,589 --> 00:54:35,921
And I won't be giving
you any, either!

1010
00:54:35,922 --> 00:54:37,022
Even gifts are fine by us, sir.

1011
00:54:37,381 --> 00:54:38,922
- What do you say, Madam?
- Of course.

1012
00:54:41,339 --> 00:54:43,131
If you withdraw
those petitions quickly...

1013
00:54:43,672 --> 00:54:44,726
it'll be better
for everyone involved.

1014
00:54:45,131 --> 00:54:46,381
Sir, are you threatening us?

1015
00:54:46,839 --> 00:54:50,006
Look at this... He walks into our court
and tries to threaten us!

1016
00:54:50,540 --> 00:54:51,287
What a joke!

1017
00:54:52,131 --> 00:54:53,255
What, sir?

1018
00:54:53,256 --> 00:54:54,506
We are rowdies first.

1019
00:54:55,297 --> 00:54:56,463
All this came after that.

1020
00:54:56,464 --> 00:54:57,588
Know your place
before you speak.

1021
00:54:57,589 --> 00:54:58,713
Madam, make your move.

1022
00:54:58,714 --> 00:55:00,213
Nothing is moving!

1023
00:55:00,214 --> 00:55:01,297
Very well.

1024
00:55:02,256 --> 00:55:03,296
- Binu.
- Huh?

1025
00:55:03,297 --> 00:55:05,258
Go wait with your father at the temple.
I'll meet you there.

1026
00:55:06,756 --> 00:55:08,006
My name is Saravanan.

1027
00:55:12,089 --> 00:55:13,409
But people know me
by another name as well.

1028
00:56:34,547 --> 00:56:35,324
Done.

1029
00:56:37,506 --> 00:56:38,963
I won't tell anyone.

1030
00:56:40,756 --> 00:56:41,364
I know!

1031
00:56:49,922 --> 00:56:50,758
Hello! Hello!

1032
00:56:51,464 --> 00:56:53,296
Hey, Baby Kannan!

1033
00:56:53,297 --> 00:56:54,463
You're going too far!

1034
00:56:54,464 --> 00:56:55,671
Should I just finish you off?

1035
00:56:55,672 --> 00:56:56,839
What did You do in there?

1036
00:56:57,797 --> 00:56:59,756
- Just "God things," bro!
- Bro! Bro!

1037
00:57:00,214 --> 00:57:01,214
What was our agreement?

1038
00:57:02,147 --> 00:57:04,177
We agreed You'd get them
justice the honest way, right?

1039
00:57:04,339 --> 00:57:05,547
And that means...

1040
00:57:05,881 --> 00:57:07,506
It's not just about
avoiding bribes...

1041
00:57:07,881 --> 00:57:09,963
You can't use your powers,
or reveal Your true identity!

1042
00:57:09,964 --> 00:57:11,130
I didn't tell a soul!

1043
00:57:11,131 --> 00:57:12,922
Promise me You won't use
Your powers again.

1044
00:57:13,422 --> 00:57:14,422
Get lost!

1045
00:57:14,589 --> 00:57:17,005
Hey! You're a God!
You used your powers!

1046
00:57:17,006 --> 00:57:18,375
What's an ordinary man
supposed to do?

1047
00:57:19,089 --> 00:57:20,089
Promise me.

1048
00:57:23,047 --> 00:57:23,319
What?

1049
00:57:24,422 --> 00:57:24,876
God?

1050
00:57:25,672 --> 00:57:26,642
Isn't that the whole challenge?

1051
00:57:27,672 --> 00:57:28,714
Are You scared?

1052
00:57:33,172 --> 00:57:34,756
No more using Your powers!

1053
00:57:59,806 --> 00:58:01,806
Here, if anyone
wants to win a case,

1054
00:58:02,167 --> 00:58:04,375
they grind chillies and smear them
on that deity's head.

1055
00:58:04,922 --> 00:58:05,922
Didn't you do it?

1056
00:58:06,547 --> 00:58:08,880
They've already ground enough
chillies on my head, right?

1057
00:58:08,881 --> 00:58:10,796
Should I really go and
do the same to Him?

1058
00:58:10,797 --> 00:58:13,005
I have a feeling He also
came here to fight a case...

1059
00:58:13,006 --> 00:58:13,617
and just ended up as a statue.

1060
00:58:14,506 --> 00:58:19,131
[devotional song plays]

1061
00:58:20,637 --> 00:58:21,279
Hi!!

1062
00:58:23,131 --> 00:58:23,931
I'll come there.

1063
00:58:27,256 --> 00:58:28,256
What do you want?

1064
00:58:30,047 --> 00:58:31,589
So, God appears before me...

1065
00:58:31,839 --> 00:58:33,381
and asks me what boon I want?

1066
00:58:34,422 --> 00:58:35,781
- Yes!
- Fine... then here's what I want!

1067
00:58:39,172 --> 00:58:39,584
Ready!

1068
00:58:40,422 --> 00:58:43,338
This old court should be transformed into
a brand-new, posh, modern complex.

1069
00:58:43,339 --> 00:58:45,630
With AC, computers, escalators,
and every modern facility imaginable!

1070
00:58:45,631 --> 00:58:47,964
It should be as high-tech
as a Google or Apple office.

1071
00:58:48,214 --> 00:58:50,088
All 27,000 cases
that are dragging on now

1072
00:58:50,089 --> 00:58:52,755
should be wrapped up completely...
as if they never even existed!

1073
00:58:52,756 --> 00:58:54,671
As for those lawyers who live off lies...

1074
00:58:54,672 --> 00:58:57,838
From now on, they should stammer
the moment they try to lie in court...

1075
00:58:57,839 --> 00:58:59,997
and fail miserably!!
[Preethi's voice echoes]

1076
00:59:05,256 --> 00:59:06,464
Chetta, the train has arrived!

1077
00:59:07,047 --> 00:59:09,046
- Cute!
- Hey, why are You leaving without a word?

1078
00:59:09,047 --> 00:59:09,538
Hello!

1079
00:59:13,631 --> 00:59:14,155
Hi!

1080
00:59:16,589 --> 00:59:18,088
Why are you with them?

1081
00:59:18,089 --> 00:59:19,495
I've got some work to do
where they're staying.

1082
00:59:20,756 --> 00:59:22,421
He knows our court inside out.

1083
00:59:22,422 --> 00:59:23,634
He's been there
for thirty years now.

1084
00:59:24,381 --> 00:59:26,714
If you need any more help,
you can always ask me too.

1085
00:59:42,214 --> 00:59:44,296
What, sir?
New to the court, huh?

1086
00:59:44,297 --> 00:59:46,088
Heard you caused
quite a stir in there today.

1087
00:59:46,089 --> 00:59:48,547
- Do you get angry easily, sir?
- Terrifyingly so.

1088
00:59:49,422 --> 00:59:51,922
Jump off while the train's still moving.
I'm saying this for your own good.

1089
00:59:54,214 --> 00:59:55,380
What, Preethi Madam?

1090
00:59:55,381 --> 00:59:56,921
You're hyping him up
way too much!

1091
00:59:56,922 --> 00:59:57,776
Just wait and see, Baldy!

1092
01:00:01,297 --> 01:00:03,130
Why are you sitting there
all stiff and tough?

1093
01:00:03,131 --> 01:00:04,547
- Gym body, huh?
- Sir, sir!

1094
01:00:04,797 --> 01:00:06,506
- Why create a scene here, sir...
- Hey!

1095
01:00:16,214 --> 01:00:17,214
Pick up those peanuts.

1096
01:00:21,797 --> 01:00:22,399
Pick them up!

1097
01:00:31,297 --> 01:00:34,131
What, sir?
Counting to ten in your head to stay calm?

1098
01:00:36,589 --> 01:00:38,130
Hey, I'm talking to you.

1099
01:00:38,131 --> 01:00:39,588
And you're fidgeting with a pen?

1100
01:00:39,589 --> 01:00:40,505
Peak...

1101
01:00:40,506 --> 01:00:41,546
mayhem...

1102
01:00:41,547 --> 01:00:42,547
loading!

1103
01:00:43,964 --> 01:00:45,546
♪ The beat of the drum,
The strike leaves you numb ♪

1104
01:00:45,547 --> 01:00:47,131
♪ The midnight raid,
A festival crusade ♪

1105
01:00:50,422 --> 01:00:51,963
♪ The death strike,
The sudden spike ♪

1106
01:00:51,964 --> 01:00:55,547
♪ The one who dared to glare at me,
Never opened his eyes again, for eternity ♪

1107
01:01:01,339 --> 01:01:02,631
Wreck them, Saamy!

1108
01:01:03,131 --> 01:01:05,005
♪ Wham, boom, kaboom! The blows fall,
Was my beating not enough for you all? ♪

1109
01:01:05,006 --> 01:01:06,338
♪ None I've struck
have survived the brawl ♪

1110
01:01:06,339 --> 01:01:09,964
♪ To harm a Lion, you'd dare to scheme?
No winner has lived to fulfil that dream ♪

1111
01:01:10,797 --> 01:01:12,589
Hey, what's with this guy?

1112
01:01:13,047 --> 01:01:14,391
He's just frozen like a statue.

1113
01:01:14,797 --> 01:01:15,956
And people were actually
scared of him?

1114
01:01:21,756 --> 01:01:23,339
Hey Baldy! Aren't you dead yet?

1115
01:01:25,589 --> 01:01:26,659
Wait, so there's no fight?

1116
01:01:35,756 --> 01:01:36,634
Baby Sir!

1117
01:01:37,464 --> 01:01:38,782
He's not worth our energy.

1118
01:01:39,506 --> 01:01:40,646
Total waste of time!

1119
01:01:46,422 --> 01:01:49,255
Sir, don't keep him here just because
he likes the room.

1120
01:01:49,256 --> 01:01:50,800
Finish the case and send him home, sir.
Poor man.

1121
01:01:52,464 --> 01:01:54,130
Binu, aren't you coming to eat?

1122
01:01:54,131 --> 01:01:55,963
No, I don't feel like it.
I'm not hungry.

1123
01:01:55,964 --> 01:01:57,464
Should I order from somewhere else?

1124
01:01:57,631 --> 01:01:59,130
There's a place right near the court.

1125
01:01:59,131 --> 01:02:00,422
The biryani there is superb!

1126
01:02:01,589 --> 01:02:03,631
- What?
- I know that place!

1127
01:02:03,881 --> 01:02:05,130
I've been there so many times.

1128
01:02:05,131 --> 01:02:08,131
In the last four months, I've spent
two lakhs on biryani from there.

1129
01:02:10,922 --> 01:02:12,476
And every single one was eaten
by your lawyers!

1130
01:02:13,047 --> 01:02:14,626
But we never had a single bite.

1131
01:02:16,164 --> 01:02:17,622
Do you know what I really wish for?

1132
01:02:18,006 --> 01:02:19,152
Once all this is finally over,

1133
01:02:19,631 --> 01:02:20,373
just once...

1134
01:02:21,589 --> 01:02:22,335
with my dad,

1135
01:02:22,839 --> 01:02:24,803
I just want to sit there
and eat a biryani in peace.

1136
01:02:26,547 --> 01:02:28,221
You guys eat there all the time.

1137
01:02:28,797 --> 01:02:30,515
I want to see what all
the hype is about.

1138
01:02:33,839 --> 01:02:35,713
See, once all these
problems are behind us,

1139
01:02:35,714 --> 01:02:38,069
once you get the gold back,
and you're healthy again,

1140
01:02:38,297 --> 01:02:40,506
you're going to that shop
to have that biryani.

1141
01:02:40,714 --> 01:02:42,213
And I'll be there to watch you.

1142
01:02:42,214 --> 01:02:44,537
I have no hope of ever getting
the gold back from this court.

1143
01:02:45,547 --> 01:02:48,005
When the gold was lost,
didn't you feel hopeless?

1144
01:02:48,006 --> 01:02:49,882
It was the police
who found it, right?

1145
01:02:50,131 --> 01:02:51,866
The same way, you'll get it
back through the court too.

1146
01:02:52,381 --> 01:02:53,778
Yeah, right!
The police didn't do squat!

1147
01:02:55,297 --> 01:02:58,381
I'm sorry...
I apologise for him hitting you.

1148
01:02:58,589 --> 01:03:01,214
My daughter's life
depends on that gold!

1149
01:03:01,589 --> 01:03:04,089
Without it...
she can't have her surgery.

1150
01:03:04,464 --> 01:03:06,597
I know none of you took it.

1151
01:03:07,256 --> 01:03:08,665
But if by any chance
you do have it...

1152
01:03:09,881 --> 01:03:11,006
Please!

1153
01:03:11,131 --> 01:03:12,506
Please, give it back.

1154
01:03:12,672 --> 01:03:14,256
Give it back...
for my daughter's sake.

1155
01:03:18,256 --> 01:03:20,631
We did it, sir!
The gold is at my aunt's place.

1156
01:03:20,922 --> 01:03:22,713
Please take it and give it
to him right away.

1157
01:03:22,714 --> 01:03:24,046
He said it's for a surgery!

1158
01:03:24,047 --> 01:03:26,406
Hey! You've already said that.
Why do you keep going on about it?

1159
01:03:26,881 --> 01:03:27,881
Go sit back down!

1160
01:03:29,422 --> 01:03:30,422
I'm sure of it!

1161
01:03:31,214 --> 01:03:33,422
Those boys must have returned
the gold themselves.

1162
01:03:33,964 --> 01:03:35,881
The compassion those boys had...

1163
01:03:36,339 --> 01:03:37,994
Not the police... not the court...

1164
01:03:38,297 --> 01:03:39,839
Not even the people here have it.

1165
01:03:40,172 --> 01:03:41,167
What kind of a place is this?

1166
01:03:41,922 --> 01:03:42,964
Disgusting!

1167
01:03:49,006 --> 01:03:49,765
What's your prayer?

1168
01:03:50,214 --> 01:03:52,459
My client's gold ornaments were
stolen on the 2nd of February.

1169
01:03:53,089 --> 01:03:55,809
The police recovered them on the 6th
and produced it before this court.

1170
01:03:56,839 --> 01:03:58,964
Today marks four months
since it was produced.

1171
01:03:59,589 --> 01:04:01,171
Yet, to this day... that gold...

1172
01:04:01,172 --> 01:04:03,160
My client has been unable
to get it back from this court.

1173
01:04:06,464 --> 01:04:08,546
The police missed four hearings
and the appraiser didn't turn up for one.

1174
01:04:08,547 --> 01:04:10,672
Two hearings were lost to strikes,
followed by a month-long court vacation.

1175
01:04:11,381 --> 01:04:12,579
And finally... for the next hearing,

1176
01:04:13,672 --> 01:04:14,286
... didn't turn up.

1177
01:04:15,297 --> 01:04:16,755
Everyone is present today.

1178
01:04:16,756 --> 01:04:18,088
At least today, my client...

1179
01:04:18,089 --> 01:04:20,506
should get his gold back.
That's my prayer.

1180
01:04:20,756 --> 01:04:23,630
This is no prayer. This is an accusation
against me and this court!

1181
01:04:23,631 --> 01:04:25,588
This is neither an accusation
nor an allegation!

1182
01:04:25,589 --> 01:04:26,839
- Just facts!
- Hey!

1183
01:04:28,339 --> 01:04:29,346
Can't you get any of this fixed?

1184
01:04:29,797 --> 01:04:32,047
- I'm checking, sir!
- Enough of this yapping!

1185
01:04:32,297 --> 01:04:33,589
Go and see what's wrong!

1186
01:04:34,297 --> 01:04:35,297
They are checking, sir!

1187
01:04:36,672 --> 01:04:38,171
What did you say? Fact?

1188
01:04:38,172 --> 01:04:39,505
Do you know what the fact is?

1189
01:04:39,506 --> 01:04:41,755
The fact is, you clearly don't
know this court's procedure!

1190
01:04:41,756 --> 01:04:43,171
Does this gold
actually belong to them?

1191
01:04:43,172 --> 01:04:45,588
Is it original?
Have they produced the bill?

1192
01:04:45,589 --> 01:04:47,796
Or is this gold linked
to any other criminal case?

1193
01:04:47,797 --> 01:04:49,671
Have they got
the customs clearance certificate?

1194
01:04:49,672 --> 01:04:50,921
Where are all these records?

1195
01:04:50,922 --> 01:04:53,338
Without all this, can it be returned
just because you ask?

1196
01:04:53,339 --> 01:04:54,796
Didn't they teach you any of this
back in Madurai court?

1197
01:04:54,797 --> 01:04:56,269
Fine, let's put that aside.
That is just procedure.

1198
01:04:56,797 --> 01:04:58,213
But this court also has
its own etiquette.

1199
01:04:58,214 --> 01:05:01,171
If you knew that, you'd have advised
your client before bringing her here.

1200
01:05:01,172 --> 01:05:02,465
Is this any way to dress
for a court?

1201
01:05:03,547 --> 01:05:05,672
Hey, girl! Where's the arm?
The arm!

1202
01:05:06,797 --> 01:05:08,506
The sleeve!
Where is the sleeve?

1203
01:05:10,006 --> 01:05:11,338
A court has its own decorum!

1204
01:05:11,339 --> 01:05:13,671
Coming here in such skimpy clothes,
wearing these flashy colours...

1205
01:05:13,672 --> 01:05:15,505
I will not entertain
these things in my court.

1206
01:05:15,506 --> 01:05:17,631
Everyone says this court
is full of problems.

1207
01:05:17,756 --> 01:05:19,464
- But you don't see any of that.
- Dear!

1208
01:05:20,297 --> 01:05:22,172
All you can see
is my dress, isn't it?

1209
01:05:22,547 --> 01:05:24,921
Then the problem isn't my clothes...
it's your perspective.

1210
01:05:24,922 --> 01:05:26,006
Dear...

1211
01:05:35,339 --> 01:05:37,838
For appearing before this court
in improper attire,

1212
01:05:37,839 --> 01:05:40,880
for contempt of court,
and for setting an improper example,

1213
01:05:40,881 --> 01:05:43,797
she is hereby sentenced
to one full day of imprisonment.

1214
01:05:44,589 --> 01:05:45,668
This shouldn't have happened!

1215
01:05:46,047 --> 01:05:47,755
It's because of me that you--

1216
01:05:47,756 --> 01:05:48,907
I only asked a fair question,
didn't I?

1217
01:05:51,464 --> 01:05:53,609
They behave like this only because
no one ever questions them!

1218
01:06:30,006 --> 01:06:30,589
Binu!

1219
01:06:34,740 --> 01:06:35,360
Binu!!

1220
01:06:44,006 --> 01:06:45,756
My child! Binu!

1221
01:06:49,172 --> 01:06:50,172
My child!

1222
01:06:50,922 --> 01:06:52,005
Binu!

1223
01:06:52,006 --> 01:06:53,464
Move aside!

1224
01:06:54,506 --> 01:06:56,381
Binu! My dear!

1225
01:06:59,172 --> 01:07:00,381
Move aside!

1226
01:07:03,256 --> 01:07:04,631
Binu!

1227
01:07:16,464 --> 01:07:17,859
There is severe internal bleeding.

1228
01:07:18,381 --> 01:07:20,714
The liver is almost 90% damaged.

1229
01:07:21,047 --> 01:07:22,756
She could slip into a coma
at any moment.

1230
01:07:22,922 --> 01:07:24,881
We must proceed with the
transplant immediately.

1231
01:07:27,089 --> 01:07:29,922
I don't care how... just send me
some money, somehow!

1232
01:07:30,089 --> 01:07:32,214
She is in a critical state.

1233
01:07:32,797 --> 01:07:35,922
I know you helped before, but
who else can I turn to but you?

1234
01:07:36,214 --> 01:07:37,381
I need that money right now.

1235
01:07:37,506 --> 01:07:40,131
You're gambling with my child's life!
Remember that!

1236
01:07:40,672 --> 01:07:41,516
Hey! Hello?

1237
01:07:42,631 --> 01:07:43,043
Hello?

1238
01:07:43,672 --> 01:07:44,203
Hello?

1239
01:07:50,672 --> 01:07:53,463
I've paid whatever I had
to get the procedure started.

1240
01:07:53,464 --> 01:07:56,047
But for the surgery to happen,
we absolutely need that gold.

1241
01:07:58,714 --> 01:08:00,213
During an emergency like this,

1242
01:08:00,214 --> 01:08:03,211
we can go to the Magistrate's house
at any hour to get an order.

1243
01:08:03,547 --> 01:08:04,432
Shall we try that?

1244
01:08:08,089 --> 01:08:09,546
Look at those politicians.

1245
01:08:09,547 --> 01:08:11,380
They rush here in the middle of the night
to get orders...

1246
01:08:11,381 --> 01:08:12,880
just to convene a general body
or shut down some committee.

1247
01:08:12,881 --> 01:08:14,130
As if those are actual emergencies!

1248
01:08:14,131 --> 01:08:15,546
Madam! Madam!
Where do you think you're going?

1249
01:08:15,547 --> 01:08:17,171
It's about a case
His Honour is already hearing.

1250
01:08:17,172 --> 01:08:19,422
It's urgent.
The girl is in the ICU.

1251
01:08:19,547 --> 01:08:21,796
So, we just need to see him,
get the order, and leave.

1252
01:08:21,797 --> 01:08:23,380
Madam, you know this, right?

1253
01:08:23,381 --> 01:08:25,463
- You can't see him at this hour.
- Will he see only them?

1254
01:08:25,464 --> 01:08:26,964
Sir, that's different...
this is different.

1255
01:08:27,089 --> 01:08:28,213
Please... we only need two minutes.

1256
01:08:28,214 --> 01:08:29,671
We'll see him
and leave immediately.

1257
01:08:29,672 --> 01:08:31,338
Madam, please understand.

1258
01:08:31,339 --> 01:08:33,421
This will cause trouble for me.
Please leave now.

1259
01:08:33,422 --> 01:08:35,339
- Hey Satti, what is the commotion?
- Sir?

1260
01:08:35,464 --> 01:08:36,142
My Lord!

1261
01:08:36,672 --> 01:08:38,671
It's regarding that
Return of Property case, My Lord.

1262
01:08:38,672 --> 01:08:40,713
The girl is in the ICU.
Her condition is critical.

1263
01:08:40,714 --> 01:08:42,505
The surgery can only happen
if we get the gold.

1264
01:08:42,506 --> 01:08:44,380
We've even brought the Customs report
that you asked for.

1265
01:08:44,381 --> 01:08:45,797
Kindly pass the order.

1266
01:08:46,047 --> 01:08:47,838
Hey, do you just let
anyone walk in like this?

1267
01:08:47,839 --> 01:08:49,671
Whatever it is, tell them
to come to court in the morning.

1268
01:08:49,672 --> 01:08:51,380
Please! Please, My Lord!
Please help--

1269
01:08:51,381 --> 01:08:52,421
Two minutes.

1270
01:08:52,422 --> 01:08:53,588
If you aren't gone by then,

1271
01:08:53,589 --> 01:08:54,963
I'll have you arrested
for trespassing.

1272
01:08:54,964 --> 01:08:57,214
Don't vent your grudge against me
on that innocent girl.

1273
01:08:58,256 --> 01:09:00,631
- Two minutes!
- My Lord! My Lord! Please!

1274
01:09:01,339 --> 01:09:03,089
Madam! Please leave!

1275
01:09:03,214 --> 01:09:05,463
He'll literally set a two-minute timer
and come back to check.

1276
01:09:05,464 --> 01:09:06,506
Please go, Madam.

1277
01:09:07,547 --> 01:09:09,506
I hope you won't take this
the wrong way...

1278
01:09:10,006 --> 01:09:11,797
Why are you begging
these people for help?

1279
01:09:12,214 --> 01:09:14,422
You have the power to do
whatever you want, don't you?

1280
01:09:29,631 --> 01:09:31,797
Sir, all the reports
have been submitted.

1281
01:09:32,089 --> 01:09:33,588
As instructed, I have
produced the DA report

1282
01:09:33,589 --> 01:09:35,380
confirming that this gold
has no link to Customs.

1283
01:09:35,381 --> 01:09:37,713
I request the court to return
the gold to my client immediately.

1284
01:09:37,714 --> 01:09:38,839
That's all!

1285
01:09:42,381 --> 01:09:43,029
"That's all?"

1286
01:09:44,964 --> 01:09:46,255
What do you mean, "That's all?"

1287
01:09:46,256 --> 01:09:48,671
What do you mean, "That's all?"
Who do you think you're talking to?

1288
01:09:48,672 --> 01:09:50,421
Some Madasamy or Kuppusamy
walking on the street?

1289
01:09:50,422 --> 01:09:52,005
I've been watching you
since you walked in here.

1290
01:09:52,006 --> 01:09:54,338
Not once have you addressed
this court with proper respect!

1291
01:09:54,339 --> 01:09:55,352
And you just say "That's all?"

1292
01:09:56,797 --> 01:09:59,056
There are specific terms used
to address a judge with respect.

1293
01:10:00,047 --> 01:10:02,214
My Lord! Lordship!
Your Honour!

1294
01:10:02,506 --> 01:10:03,834
You haven't used even one of them!

1295
01:10:04,214 --> 01:10:07,296
So you've come here with a plan
to insult this court, haven't you?

1296
01:10:07,297 --> 01:10:07,963
Sir! Sir!

1297
01:10:07,964 --> 01:10:09,756
- It's not like that, sir.
- Did I ask you?

1298
01:10:11,006 --> 01:10:12,400
Speak only when you're spoken to.
Do you understand?

1299
01:10:14,756 --> 01:10:15,963
For insulting the court,

1300
01:10:15,964 --> 01:10:18,047
you will first apologise. Then you
may take your client's gold and leave.

1301
01:10:18,714 --> 01:10:21,011
You must address this court
with respect and apologise.

1302
01:10:27,422 --> 01:10:29,297
What? Should I pass on the case?

1303
01:10:29,714 --> 01:10:30,272
Huh?

1304
01:10:31,089 --> 01:10:32,338
Don't waste the court's time!

1305
01:10:32,339 --> 01:10:33,631
Hey! Call the next case!

1306
01:10:41,089 --> 01:10:42,217
I am sorry...

1307
01:10:45,506 --> 01:10:46,672
My Lord!

1308
01:11:24,672 --> 01:11:26,691
Get everything ready
for the surgery. I'll be there soon.

1309
01:11:28,006 --> 01:11:29,159
I am on my way to the hospital.

1310
01:11:31,464 --> 01:11:31,859
What?

1311
01:11:33,839 --> 01:11:34,476
What?

1312
01:11:36,672 --> 01:11:37,156
Okay!

1313
01:11:38,297 --> 01:11:38,697
Oh!

1314
01:11:39,589 --> 01:11:39,936
Oh!

1315
01:11:45,047 --> 01:11:49,505
♪ Why did she go away? ♪

1316
01:11:49,506 --> 01:11:55,463
♪ Where did she depart
without a word to say? ♪

1317
01:11:55,464 --> 01:12:01,631
♪ Why did she fade
into the shadows away? ♪

1318
01:12:17,172 --> 01:12:18,256
What's up, Chetta?

1319
01:12:20,089 --> 01:12:21,631
Looks like you won the case, huh?

1320
01:12:24,881 --> 01:12:26,505
See if you can do
something for us too...

1321
01:12:26,506 --> 01:12:27,797
You'll do the needful, right?

1322
01:12:27,964 --> 01:12:29,381
Shall I do the "needful" to you?

1323
01:12:30,881 --> 01:12:31,964
I won.

1324
01:12:32,589 --> 01:12:33,797
I won the case.

1325
01:12:34,422 --> 01:12:35,464
Here!

1326
01:12:36,047 --> 01:12:37,172
Take your fee!

1327
01:12:41,631 --> 01:12:42,839
Go!

1328
01:12:43,297 --> 01:12:44,297
I won!

1329
01:12:45,256 --> 01:12:48,463
♪ Oh, my little princess ♪

1330
01:12:48,464 --> 01:12:51,880
♪ I failed you... I confess ♪

1331
01:12:51,881 --> 01:12:55,631
♪ I gave you hope,
then let it stray ♪

1332
01:12:56,047 --> 01:12:57,256
I won the case!

1333
01:12:59,214 --> 01:13:00,838
But my daughter is gone!

1334
01:13:00,839 --> 01:13:03,171
♪ Oh, my little princess ♪

1335
01:13:03,172 --> 01:13:06,463
♪ I failed you... I confess ♪

1336
01:13:06,464 --> 01:13:10,463
♪ I gave you hope,
then let it stray ♪

1337
01:13:10,464 --> 01:13:15,006
♪ My princess,
why did you go away? ♪

1338
01:13:15,922 --> 01:13:19,047
My daughter is gone,
you bloody scavenger!

1339
01:13:19,214 --> 01:13:20,422
My daughter is gone!

1340
01:13:21,756 --> 01:13:22,756
She is dead!

1341
01:13:29,131 --> 01:13:30,839
My daughter Binu is dead!

1342
01:13:40,631 --> 01:13:41,396
What is it, sir?

1343
01:13:42,089 --> 01:13:43,506
Are you here looking for a lawyer?

1344
01:13:43,631 --> 01:13:45,339
Run! Save yourself
and get out of here!

1345
01:13:46,672 --> 01:13:48,922
Advocate... do you want some biryani?

1346
01:13:49,381 --> 01:13:50,381
Do you want a smoke?

1347
01:13:50,714 --> 01:13:53,131
Don't you need to eat?
Here's your fee! Take it!

1348
01:13:53,339 --> 01:13:54,401
- Take it!
- Sir!

1349
01:13:57,214 --> 01:13:58,214
Sir!

1350
01:13:58,714 --> 01:13:59,714
Lawyer sir!

1351
01:14:02,464 --> 01:14:05,464
Why did you get
this gold back for me, sir?

1352
01:14:06,047 --> 01:14:07,422
My child is dead, sir!

1353
01:14:07,922 --> 01:14:09,547
My daughter is dead!

1354
01:14:10,047 --> 01:14:11,339
She's gone, sir...

1355
01:14:13,756 --> 01:14:15,172
What do I even need this for now?

1356
01:14:15,672 --> 01:14:17,464
You keep it, sir.

1357
01:14:18,131 --> 01:14:19,381
Just keep it for yourself.

1358
01:14:20,714 --> 01:14:23,089
I don't know how to use
Google Pay, sir.

1359
01:14:24,089 --> 01:14:25,839
I don't even know how
to use Google Pay...

1360
01:14:26,172 --> 01:14:29,755
♪ I failed you... I confess ♪

1361
01:14:29,756 --> 01:14:33,463
♪ I gave you hope,
then let it stray ♪

1362
01:14:33,464 --> 01:14:37,922
♪ My princess,
why did you go away? ♪

1363
01:14:45,381 --> 01:14:48,696
♪ Karuppu is my favourite colour ♪

1364
01:14:49,756 --> 01:14:51,222
You worked so hard
to get his gold back...

1365
01:14:51,672 --> 01:14:53,002
and he walks away
after grabbing Your collar!

1366
01:14:53,547 --> 01:14:55,368
That's why You shouldn't
do good for people like this!

1367
01:14:56,381 --> 01:14:57,672
Still... it's a pity, isn't it?

1368
01:14:58,131 --> 01:15:00,046
His only daughter...
such a young girl.

1369
01:15:00,047 --> 01:15:01,588
I would've made them
run in circles, sure...

1370
01:15:01,589 --> 01:15:03,006
but I wouldn't have let her die.

1371
01:15:03,547 --> 01:15:04,671
Why are You glaring at me?

1372
01:15:04,672 --> 01:15:06,213
You came to His Lordship's
house last night, right?

1373
01:15:06,214 --> 01:15:08,213
If You had done the needful,

1374
01:15:08,214 --> 01:15:10,297
he'd have passed the order
without holding a grudge.

1375
01:15:12,047 --> 01:15:14,213
Good Heavens! I was actually
shaking with fear...

1376
01:15:14,214 --> 01:15:16,131
thinking I was going up
against God Himself.

1377
01:15:16,256 --> 01:15:18,297
But my court didn't let me
down, did it?

1378
01:15:20,506 --> 01:15:22,088
It's exactly what
I said that day.

1379
01:15:22,089 --> 01:15:23,881
This court has its own procedure.

1380
01:15:24,047 --> 01:15:25,805
Even if God Himself shows up,
nothing changes.

1381
01:15:26,381 --> 01:15:28,214
My dear brother,
the challenge is over.

1382
01:15:28,339 --> 01:15:29,486
Shut the shrine and clear out.

1383
01:15:30,047 --> 01:15:30,759
This death...

1384
01:15:31,381 --> 01:15:32,416
it isn't on me.

1385
01:15:32,922 --> 01:15:34,124
It's on You.

1386
01:15:34,422 --> 01:15:36,214
Remember when You said
"God things"?

1387
01:15:36,422 --> 01:15:37,881
Well, this...
is "Just court things!"

1388
01:15:38,881 --> 01:15:39,881
Bro!

1389
01:15:58,797 --> 01:16:00,088
Please... just leave me alone.

1390
01:16:00,089 --> 01:16:02,716
I didn't know you were part of
Baby Kannan's team when I came to you.

1391
01:16:02,881 --> 01:16:04,656
I've already given you
all the money you asked for.

1392
01:16:05,589 --> 01:16:07,714
I have nothing left to give.

1393
01:16:08,297 --> 01:16:09,921
Please, just give me my evidence...

1394
01:16:09,922 --> 01:16:11,672
and my case files.

1395
01:16:12,006 --> 01:16:13,714
I'll find another lawyer.

1396
01:16:15,589 --> 01:16:16,631
Please.

1397
01:16:16,922 --> 01:16:18,422
I'll give you one last chance.

1398
01:16:34,047 --> 01:16:37,131
You heard this once.
I'll say it again.

1399
01:16:37,881 --> 01:16:39,713
Three-quarters of the people
here are lawyers.

1400
01:16:39,714 --> 01:16:42,922
If even one of them dares
to touch that file, I'll drop your case.

1401
01:16:43,339 --> 01:16:46,006
Otherwise, you'll just have
to withdraw it.

1402
01:16:54,881 --> 01:16:57,755
- Sir, please take up my case, sir.
- Don't drag me into trouble. Go, dear.

1403
01:16:57,756 --> 01:16:59,631
Sir, please help me.
Please, sir.

1404
01:17:02,506 --> 01:17:03,506
Sister...

1405
01:17:03,839 --> 01:17:05,547
Please, at least you can help me.

1406
01:17:06,589 --> 01:17:07,631
Sister!

1407
01:17:25,047 --> 01:17:26,672
Did you lose as a God?

1408
01:17:27,464 --> 01:17:28,756
No... you lost as a human.

1409
01:17:30,006 --> 01:17:32,006
And humans losing here
is nothing new.

1410
01:17:32,172 --> 01:17:35,422
Every single day,
thousands of people lose in this court.

1411
01:17:37,214 --> 01:17:40,546
Then I shall be
the last human to lose here.

1412
01:17:40,547 --> 01:17:43,714
From this day forward, no one seeking
justice in this court shall ever lose.

1413
01:17:44,631 --> 01:17:46,297
I won't let them lose.
Not on my watch.

1414
01:19:22,464 --> 01:19:24,755
♪ He's a tiger that roars
like sudden thunder ♪

1415
01:19:24,756 --> 01:19:27,005
♪ He's the one who'll tear
your pride asunder ♪

1416
01:19:27,006 --> 01:19:29,297
♪ With fireworks raging,
burning in wrath ♪

1417
01:19:31,381 --> 01:19:33,213
♪ With steely defiance ♪

1418
01:19:33,214 --> 01:19:35,505
♪ He counts every bone,
no mercy, no compliance ♪

1419
01:19:35,506 --> 01:19:37,671
♪ Behold the God of Death
before you ♪

1420
01:19:37,672 --> 01:19:40,172
♪ Look, Death himself stands
in your view ♪

1421
01:19:40,381 --> 01:19:43,005
♪ At a single stare ♪

1422
01:19:43,006 --> 01:19:47,464
♪ You shatter and scatter
silently in the air ♪

